31<lb/> <head>- Hunting Plum Pudding. -</head> <lb/> 1 lb of Suet chopped fine, 1 lb grated bread, 1 lb sugar<lb/> 1 lb of Rasins, &amp; 1 lb of Currants, then yolks of 12<lb/> eggs, a little candid peal + nutmeg, + what Brandy<lb/> you please. This quantity should boil 12 hours.<lb/> <head>- A Superfine Plum Pudding. -</head><lb/> Take 4 ozs. of grounded pudding biscuit, + 2 ozs. of the<lb/> best four (or good common biscuit) 1/2 lb of bloom<lb/> or muscated rasins stoned, the same quantity of<lb/> fresh Lante currants picked and plumped, 1/2 lb<lb/> of Suet chopped very fine, a small quantity of nut<lb/> -meg 1.4 lb of fine beat sugar, a drachm of pounded<lb/> cinnamon + 2 blades of mace, 2 ozs. of candid Lemons<lb/> a little orange + citron shied, + 2 ozs of blanched<lb/> Almonds roughly chopped. - Beat well 4 eggs<lb/> and put to them a little sweet milk, 1 glass<lb/> of white brandy, and then mix in the flour and<lb/> all the ingredients. - Tie up the pudding firm, and<lb/> boil it for 4 hours, keeping up the boil. Serve it up<lb/> with <hi rend="underline">good</hi> Brandy Sauce.<lb/> <head>Treacle Pudding</head><lb/> 1/2 lb. of Flour, 1/2 lob. of Suet, 1/2 lb. currants, 1/2 lb. of Treacle.<lb/> you may add what Plumbs you please. and then<lb/> <hi rend="underline">boil it 3 hours.</hi>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/036|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
32<lb/> <head>- Paradise Pudding. -</head> <lb/> If you'll have a nice pudding, pray mind what you<lb/> are taught. Take 2 <hi rend="superscript"><unclear>Dz</unclear></hi> worth of eggs, when they give<lb/> twelve for a groat, Take of the same fruit which<lb/> Eve once did taste, Well pared + well clipped, half<lb/> a dozen at least, Six oz's of currants, pray pick them<lb/> quite clean. Lest they grate in your teeth you know<lb/> what I <hi rend="underline">mean</hi>. Six oz's. of Sugar wont make it too sweet<lb/> Take salt and some nutmeg to make it complete,<lb/> And then you may add, if you're willing and handy<lb/> some good lemon Peel, and a good glass of <hi rend="underline">Brandy</hi><lb/> Three hours let it boil, without hurry or flutter,<lb/> And then serve it up with some good melted butter<lb/> Adam tasted this Pudding twas wonderous <unclear>nice</unclear><lb/> to Eve cut her husband another <hi rend="underline">good slice</hi>.<lb/> <head>Carrot Pudding.</head><lb/> 1/4 lb. of Rasins, 1/4 lb. of currants, 1/4 lb. of sugar, 1/4 lb. of<lb/> Suet, 1/4 lb. of Flour, 1/4 lb. of Carrots, 1/4 lb of Potatoes, boil<lb/> it four hours.<lb/> <head>Quaking Pudding _</head><lb/> 1 pint of cream, mixed with 2 spoonful of flour<lb/> 5 egg an a little salt, and sugar, boil it &amp;<lb/> mould an hour and a half
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/037|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
33<lb/> <head>- Venetian Pudding. -</head> <lb/> Soak 2 ozs. of Ratifies, + 7 Sponge Biscuits in sherry<lb/> wine, + a little Brandy, wet a pint mould with<lb/> cold water, + put in a layer of the soaked cakes,<lb/> and a layer of rich preserve until the mould<lb/> is full. - Dissolve 1/2 oz. of Isinglass, in about 3 parts<lb/> of a pint of thin cream, boil it a few minutes<lb/> + sweeten to your taste, <sic>strane</sic> it, and when<lb/> cold, add a little Brandy, + fill up your pudding<lb/> taking care the cream gets well to the <unclear>hole</unclear> of<lb/> the mould, when set turn it and the same as<lb/> Blamemange. <add>Miss M. Darlington</add><lb/> <add><hi rend="underline">Leicestershire</hi></add><lb/> <head>Bakewell Pudding</head><lb/> Line your dish or saucer with a good puff pasta<lb/> + put in a layer of preserve or jelly, then mix<lb/> together 1/4 lb of butter, 6 ozs. of sifted sugar, the<lb/> yolks of 6 egg, flavour it with almonds, + lay it<lb/> on the preserve, bake it in a moderate oven<lb/> from 20 minutes to half an hour.<lb/> <head>Citron Puddings.</head><lb/> To 1/4 a pint of cream, 1 spoonful of flour, 2 oz fine<lb/> sugar, a little nutmeg mixed well together with the
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/038|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
34<lb/> yolks of 4 eggs, put it into teacups, + stick into<lb/> it 2 ozs of citron cut very fine, bake it in a<lb/> quick oven, 30 minutes, served with Brandy<lb/> Sauce, this quantity with make four Puddings.<lb/> <head>Lemon boiled Pudding.</head><lb/> 1/2 lb of Suet, 1/2 lb of Bread, 2 eggs, the juice of a<lb/> Lemon, and the rind of 2, 2 spoonful of moist sugar<lb/> <head>Lemon Baked Pudding.</head><lb/> 1/4 lb. of Butter, 6 ozs of Sugar, the yolks of 6 eggs, the<lb/> white of three, and the rind and juice of two<lb/> Lemons, put a paste in your dish.<lb/> <head>Another Lemon Pudding.</head><lb/> 2 penny loaves grated and steeped in a pint of cream<lb/> 4 eggs, the peel, and juice of a Lemon, and sugar to yr taste<lb/> <head>Almond Pudding</head><lb/> Take the crumbs of a penny loaf, pour a small quantity<lb/> of boiling milk over it, add 6 eggs, 1/4 lb. of almonds<lb/> pounded fine, the juice + peel grated fine of 2<lb/> lemons, sweeten it to your taste, + boil it 4 hours<lb/> 2 spoonful of flour, may or may not be added.<lb/> <head>For a Pudding</head><lb/> 1/2 lb. of grated Apples, 1/4 lb. of Butter melted, 1/4 lb of Sugar<lb/> 4 eggs, the peel and juice of a Lemon, lay a puff<lb/> paste <hi rend="underline">in your dish and bake it</hi>.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

