35<lb/> <head>Biscuit Pudding</head><lb/> Half a pound of Spong biscuits 1 oz. of sweet<lb/> Almonds, 1/2 lb. of small rasins without stones, 4<lb/> eggs put a few of the Almonds, Rasins + some can-<lb/> did peel at the bottom of your mould, after<lb/> well buttering it, chop the rest of your rasins and<lb/> Almonds, lay first biscuits, and then fruit until<lb/> the mould is full, beat the eggs in a little new<lb/> milk, and pour over, just to moisten the Biscuits<lb/> then quarter of an hour will boil it, do not let<lb/> the water cover it, or it will be too soft to tease<lb/> out. Serve it with white wine sauce.<lb/> <head>A Custard Pudding</head><lb/> 1 Pint of <hi rend="underline">good</hi> milk, or thin cream, 3 eggs, 1 tablespoon<lb/> + a half of sifted sugar, 2 Tablespoonful of flour, beat<lb/> them well together, prove it into a dish lined<lb/> with paste, and any kind of sweetmeat at the<lb/> bottom, bake it half an hour, in a quick oven.<lb/> <head>Welsh Pudding</head><lb/> Melt 1/2 lb Butter by setting it in a basin floating in hot water<lb/> + <sic>gladually</sic> mix with it the yolks of 8 egg, + the white<lb/> of 4, sweeten with fine pounded sugar, + season with<lb/> grated Lemon + a little nutmeg, <unclear>Bak</unclear> it in a dish<lb/> with an <hi rend="underline">ornamented paste border.</hi>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

