36<lb/> <head>Bread Pudding</head><lb/> Pour a pint of boiling milk over what will fill a<lb/> breakfast up full of bread crumbs, let them<lb/> soak covered till cold + mash them smooth<lb/> with a spoon, sweeten it to your taste.<lb/> Add to it 4 or 5 ggs, well beat + season with<lb/> cinnamon or nutmeg, stir in 2 oz. of currants<lb/> picked + plumped or a few cut rasins, or<lb/> the pudding may be made very rich by the <lb/> addition of blanched + chopped Almonds<lb/> candid citron + orange peel, with rasins +<lb/> currants. - Boil it in a basin or bake it in a dish.<lb/> <head>To make light Puddings.</head><lb/> Flour, Sugar, Butter 2 ozs of each, a pint of cream<lb/> or new milk, the yolks of 4 eggs, + the whites of 2<lb/> the butter to be melted in a part of the milk<lb/> then flour sugar + eggs to be mixed with the<lb/> other part, when cold mix the whole up together<lb/> bake them half an hour in small pans.<lb/> <head>Baked Apple Pudding</head><lb/> Peel and quarter 4 large Apples, boil them with<lb/> the rind of a Lemon, + so little water that when done,<lb/> none shall remain, beat them fine in a mortar, add
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/041|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
37<lb/> the crumbs of a small roll, 4 ozs of butter melted,<lb/> the yolks of 5 eggs, + the whites of 3, the juice of<lb/> half a Lemon, + sugar to your taste, beat altogether<lb/> + lay in a dish with paste to turn out.<lb/> <head>Derbyshire Pudding.</head><lb/> 1 pint of milk or thin cream, 2 tablespoonful<lb/> of fine flour, mix in it the milk by degrees,<lb/> boil it till it I thick, a 1/4 lb. of loaf sugar, a little<lb/> salt, the rind of a lemon grated fine, 5 eggs<lb/> the whites of 3, put a paste in your dish, and when<lb/> baked put currant jelly on the top.<lb/> <head>A <unclear>Rick</unclear> Pudding</head><lb/> 2 ozs. of Macaroons, 2 oz of Ratifies, + 2 oz. of finger<lb/> biscuits, laid at the bottom of the dish, and custard<lb/> poured over it.<lb/> <head>Carrot Pudding</head><lb/> Take the crumbs of a small white loaf grated, 4<lb/> eggs beat up, a pint of new milk, 2 oz butter, a 1/4 lb<lb/> of currants, a little nutmeg + Lemon peel grated, sweet<lb/> -end with a white loaf sugar to your taste, mixed all<lb/> up together, + put into small cups to bake, butter the<lb/> <hi rend="underline">cups</hi> well, just before they are put in the oven, squeeze<lb/> into a little lemon juice. - Send it to table with<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Wine Sauce.</hi>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

