38<lb/> <head>Ground Rice Pudding</head><lb/> Take 6 ozs. of the flour of Rice, put it into a quart<lb/> of milk, and let it boil till it is pretty stirring it<lb/> all the time, then pour it into a pan, stir<lb/> in 1/2 a lb. of fresh butter, &amp; a 1/4 of Sugar, when cold<lb/> grate some nutmeg, beat in 6 eggs, beat + stir all<lb/> well together, lay a thin puff paste in the bottom<lb/> of your dish, pour it in &amp; bake it. The peel of a<lb/> Lemon grated, + the juice of greatly improves the <add>flavour</add>.<lb/> <head>Boiled Vermicelli Pudding</head><lb/> Stir over the fire very gently 4 ozs of Vermicelli in a<lb/> pint of new milk, until it be scalding hot, then<lb/> pour it into a basin, add to it 1 oz of butter, + 2 oz.<lb/> of sugar while hot, when the above is cold, mix in<lb/> it very gently 2 well beaten eggs and put into<lb/> a mould. - Boil it an hour.<lb/> <head>Ratific Pudding.</head><lb/> Flavour a pint and a half of milk, with 4 Bay leaves<lb/> + a little cinnamon, + four ozs of sifted sugar, when<lb/> the whole has simmered for some minutes, strain off<lb/> the milk, + stir it gradually to 6 eggs, let the mixture<lb/> cool, then add a glass of Brandy. Lay a paste round<lb/> the dish, then sprinkle into <gap/> oz. of <unclear>Ratifias</unclear>, grate<lb/> the rind of a Lemon over, and place 3 ozs. of whole
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

