39<lb/> Ratifies upon them pour in sufficient of the<lb/> custard to soak them an hour afterwards add<lb/> the remainder.<lb/> <head>Castle Pudding.</head><lb/> Take the weight of 2 eggs in butter, sugar + flour<lb/> set the butter in a basin, before the fire, till half<lb/> melted, then beat it to a cream, beat the 2 eggs for<lb/> 10 minutes, then mix them with the butter (gently)<lb/> then the sugar, then the flour, bake it in cups<lb/> in a slow oven for 20 minutes, + when baked<lb/> pour white wine over them.<lb/> <head>Curates Pudding.</head><lb/> Weigh 3 eggs, put the same quantity of flour preserved<lb/> sugar, + butter, bet the butter to a cream, with the<lb/> hand, the eggs must be well beaten + add the<lb/> above by degrees to the butter, grate in the peel of a<lb/> lemon, put in the juice, and a little nutmeg<lb/> fill 5 cups, (well buttered) with the mixture<lb/> and bake it 1/3 of an hour.<lb/> <head>For W. W. Wynne's Pudding</head><lb/> Sweet bread crumbs pounded Lump sugar of each<lb/> 1/2 lb. 2 eggs. the juice + grated rind of a Lemon<lb/> then basin to be <hi rend="underline">well</hi> lined with Rasins.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

