45<lb/> <head>Calves Foot Jelly.</head><lb/> 1 Gallon of water to 4 calves feet let it simmer<lb/> gently till tender, + reduced to 1 quart of liquor, take<lb/> them out, + put in 1/2 oz of Isinglass, then boil it gently<lb/> till it is dissolved, then put it through a hair sieve<lb/> + when quite cold, put to it 1 pint of white wine - <lb/> (cowslip will make it the best colouring) beat the<lb/> whites of 8 eggs to a froth, + put them in with the<lb/> rind + juice of 2 Lemons, add to it nearly 1/2 lt. of Loaf<lb/> sugar broke, but not sifted, then set it on the fire<lb/> for a few minutes, stirring it all the time gently till<lb/> it is cooled a little, + run it through a thick Flannel<lb/> bag into your mould, shapes, or glasses. put a thin<lb/> slice of Lemon at the bottom of your bag as it will<lb/> make the jelly run + clean the better, but in the<lb/> eggs when boiling, "Do not crack your feet at all."<lb/> <head>Port Wine Jelly</head><lb/> 1 1/2 pint of port wine, to 1 ozs. of Isinglass, let it stand<lb/> an hour to soften, then juice of half a lemon + sugar<lb/> to your taste. "Be careful it does not boil."<lb/> <head>Damson Jelly</head><lb/> Boil 1 oz. of Isinglass in 1 1/2 pints of Damson syrup, sweeten<lb/> it to your taste, then then strain it through a sieve<lb/> <hi rend="underline">"Into your moulds or Glasses."</hi>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

