46<lb/> <head>Orange Jelly</head><lb/> Take 6 large oranges, peel three of them very thin,<lb/> squeeze the juice of all upon the peel, + let it<lb/> stand all night, dissolve 1 oz. of Isinglass in a pint<lb/> of water, add to it the orange juice, strain it through<lb/> a fine strainer, and sweeten it to your taste, it should<lb/> be put in shapes, and will turn out well when cold<lb/> If the Oranges are very sweet, the juice of a Lemon add.<lb/> <head>Apple Jelly</head><lb/> Boil what quantity of apples you like, with as little<lb/> water as will cover them, boil them quite down to<lb/> a pulse, then run it through a jelly bag, + boil<lb/> the syrup 20 minutes, + add 1 1/2 lbs. of Loaf Sugar to<lb/> 1 quart of the juice, boil it till it will set, add the<lb/> rind of a Lemon, + the juice, if the apples are very flat.<lb/> <head>Currant Jelly</head><lb/> To 1 pint of syrup 1 lb. of Loaf Sugar, sifted and made<lb/> as hot as possible, then moment the syrup boils + the<lb/> scum has been removed, pour in the hot sugar<lb/> stir and boil 5 minutes, + pour into your moulds.<lb/> <head>Another receipt for Currant Jelly</head><lb/> 1 Quart of Currant juice, + 1 1/2 of Loaf Sugar, boil it<lb/> and scum it well till it will set.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/051|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
47<lb/> <head>Damson Cheese</head><lb/> Bake a quantity of Damsons and put them through<lb/> a <sic>cullinder</sic> + to every quart of pulp, which must<lb/> be boiled two hours, add 1 lb. of Loaf sugar <sic>swifted</sic> fine<lb/> + made <sic>throughly</sic> hot, and well stirred into the<lb/> Damsons. - Then just into your moulds for use.<lb/> <head>Apple Cheese</head><lb/> Take 7 lbs of apples pealed + the cores taken out, put 1 lb<lb/> of raw sugar, add 2 Lemons peeled very thin, the<lb/> peel should bee boiled with the other ingredients<lb/> but the juice of the Lemon should not be boil<lb/> them till half boiled, they should be boiled in<lb/> the same manner, and about the same time as<lb/> Damson cheese, put the apples on plates to dry<lb/> <head>Green Gooseberry Cheese</head><lb/> Weigh your fruit, + to every lb. of fruit allow 1/3 lb, of sugar<lb/> (Loaf sugar) wash the gooseberries, + throw them<lb/> into a kettle, <hi rend="underline">over a very slow fire</hi>, + let them simmer<lb/> until they will mash, put in the sugar + boil them<lb/> 1/2 an hour - <unclear>blserve</unclear> to stir them well, then put into the moulds<lb/> <head>Raspberry Cakes</head><lb/> 2 pints of raspberries, jug them about 3 hours, then take<lb/> out about half the seeds, by rubbing them through
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/052|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
48<lb/> a sieve, put the pulp to the other part<lb/> + bruise it very fine, to every lb. of fruit, put<lb/> 1/4 lb of sugar pounded + sfted, boil the raspberries<lb/> 1/2 an hour before you put the sugar to them, take<lb/> it off the fire + stir in the sugar you may then<lb/> heat it so as to melt the sugar but <hi rend="underline">mind it never</hi><lb/> <hi rend="underline">boils</hi>. - Put it on plates + when day or one <unclear>side</unclear>,<lb/> cut it in shapes + turn it on clean plates.<lb/> <head>- Gooseberry Cakes. -</head> <lb/> Take your white gooseberries, <unclear>nose</unclear> them + wash<lb/> them + add as much water as will cover them<lb/> + let it boil an 1/4 of an hour, then put it through<lb/> a sieve, set it on the fire, boil + scum it well. To an<lb/> pint of jelly put 1 lb of sugar finely sifted, + <unclear>scall</unclear><lb/> it till the sugar is melted, but do not let it boil<lb/> then put it into plates, + when it is candid at<lb/> the top lay it upon glass + turn it often, then<lb/> stronger you make it of gooseberries the better it will jelly<lb/> <head>- Gooseberry Clear Cakes. -</head> <lb/> Take a quantity of gooseberries, jug them + pour the<lb/> clear juice from them + every pint of juice put<lb/> 1 lb. of sugar sifted finely do it well before the sugar<lb/> is put in, not afterwards. run it into plates + when candid<lb/> then cut it into shapes + dry it on glass. Currants are done<lb/> in <hi rend="underline">the same way</hi>.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/053|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
49<lb/> <head>- Blanck Flange. -</head> <lb/> 1/2 oz Isinglass 6 cloves, 4 blades of mace a bit of cinnamon<lb/> a 1/4 of the rind of a small lemon pared thin, to<lb/> these put a 1/4 of a pint of boiling water, let it stand<lb/> till it is a stiff jelly then melt it over the fire<lb/> when melted put to it 1/2 a pint of good milk<lb/> two or three spoonful of Rose Water, the same<lb/> quantity of White wine, sweeten it to you taste,<lb/> then strain it off + stir it until it is quite cold<lb/> The wine must not be added <hi rend="underline">until it is taken off the fire.</hi><lb/> <head>- Clear Blank Flange. -</head> <lb/> Take a 1/4 of strong calves foot jelly, skim off the fat +<lb/> strain it, beat the whites of 4 eggs, + put them to<lb/> your jelly set it on the fire + keep stirring it till<lb/> it boils, then pour it into a jelly bag, + run it<lb/> through several times till it is clear, beat 1 oz. of<lb/> sweet almonds + 1 oz. of butter to a paste with a<lb/> spoonful of Rose water <unclear>oneegeal</unclear> through a<lb/> cloth, then mix it with the jelly + 3 spoonful<lb/> of cream set it over the fire again till it is at<lb/> - most boiling keep stirring it all the time pour<lb/> it into a bowl + stir it often till it is cold<lb/> then wet your moulds + fill them.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/054|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
50<lb/> <head>Dutch Slummery</head> <lb/> Peel 4 Lemons very thin, put the peel into a<lb/> basin + squeeze the juice upon it then put<lb/> to it 1/2 a pint of water + let it stand all night<lb/> dissolve 1 oz of Isinglass to half a pint of water<lb/> 8 ozs. of Loaf sugar sifted, 6 eggs, mix the eggs + sugar<lb/> well together with a spoon strain + put to it<lb/> the Isinglass + Lemon juice, mix all well together<lb/> set it upon the fire till it becomes thick, but<lb/> <hi rend="underline">be sure</hi> not to let it boil, stir it all the time<lb/> one way, pour it into a basin + stir it frequently<lb/> till nearly cold then pour it into your shapes<lb/> which must be wet with cold water.<lb/> <head>Another receipt for Dutch Slummery</head><lb/> 1 oz. of Isinglass, dissolved in a pint of water,<lb/> strain it, + when nearly cold the juice of 2 Lemons<lb/> + the peel of one grated the yolks of 4 eggs. 1/2 an<lb/> pint of white wine 1/4 lb. of fine sugar, let it<lb/> boil strain it + stir it till nearly cold before<lb/> you put it in your moulds.<lb/> <head>Floating Islands</head><lb/> 3 Spoonfuls of raspberry jam, the whites of 4 eggs<lb/> beat to a light froth + laid in <unclear>waves</unclear> in<lb/> sweetened cream.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/055|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
57<lb/> <head>Dulibubs. -</head> <lb/> 1 pint of good cream, 1/2 a lb. of loaf sugar, 1/2 a pint<lb/> of white wine, the rind of a lemon grated, +<lb/> the juice of it. - Add a <hi rend="underline">little</hi> Brandy.<lb/> <head>Egg Cordial</head><lb/> Put 4 spoonfuls of water, + one of brandy into a<lb/> sauce pan, with a little sugar + grated ginger<lb/> (when it is hot but not boiling) add to it an<lb/> egg well beaten set it on the fire to thicken<lb/> but be sure + not boil, serve it up with toasted bread<lb/> <head>Lemon Custard. -</head><lb/> Beat the yolks of 8 eggs, as well as if for a cake till<lb/> they are a strong white cream, mix in gradually<lb/> a pint of boiling water, + the grated rind +<lb/> juice of 2 Lemons sweeten to taste + stir one<lb/> way over the fire till it thickens, but do not<lb/> let it boil. - Add a little wine + a spoonful of<lb/> brandy, when the custard is nearly ready, stir till cool.<lb/> <head>Lemon Cream.</head><lb/> Peel 4 lemons very thin, + put them into a pint<lb/> of spring water the over night, then add the <lb/> juice of the lemons + the whites of 7 eggs, + sugar<lb/> to your taste, let the ingredients simmer over a
