52<lb/> slow fire till they thicken, then strain it thro<lb/> a jelly + put into your glasses.<lb/> <head>Apricot Cream.</head><lb/> 1/2 a pint of cream the rind of one Lemon grated<lb/> on Sugar, let it stand till the sugar is dissolved<lb/> then add the juice of the Lemon + a glass of sherry<lb/> whip it till it becomes thick + pour on their Preserves.<lb/> <head>Stoved Cream.</head><lb/> Dissolve 1/4 oz. of Isinglass in a very small quantity of<lb/> water then put to it 1 pint of cream, sweeten<lb/> it + boil it short time with cinnamon + lemon<lb/> peel, when nearly cold add ratifies + pour<lb/> it upon sweetmeats in glasses.<lb/> <head>Italian Cream.</head><lb/> In a quart of thick cream, add the juice of 4<lb/> lemons, + the rind of 2 grated, sugar to your taste<lb/> when it has stood half an hour, wisk it until<lb/> it becomes very thick, then tie it as strongly as<lb/> possible in a napkin + set it on a sieve an<lb/> whole night to drain, in the morning it will<lb/> be stiff &amp; turn out well.<lb/> <head>Another receipt for Italian Cream</head><lb/> A quart of thick cream, 3 spoonfuls of Brandy
