55<lb/> <head><sic>Strengthing</sic> Jelly</head><lb/> Take 1 oz. of Isinglass to a pint of water and<lb/> let it boil until reduced to one half the quan<lb/> -tity, then take half a breakfast cup full of<lb/> this filled up with Port wine, <sic>occassionally</sic><lb/> a little mace or cinnamon may be put in<lb/> to flavor it.<lb/> <head>Another Receipt</head><lb/> Take 2 ounces of Isinglass, half an ounce of Gum<lb/> arabic, steep them at night in a pint of<lb/> Kent or Mountain Wine then put them into<lb/> a Saucepan with 3 ounces of brown sugar candy<lb/> and a nutmeg grated simmer them together<lb/> until quite dissolved, then strain them<lb/> thro a sieve. Take a piece the use of a Nutmeg<lb/> 3 times a day in Port Wine.<lb/> <head>Cream Custards.</head><lb/> Take a pint of good cream 2 oz. of loaf<lb/> sugar melt over a slow fire, beat the<lb/> yolks of 5 eggs stir them in by degrees<lb/> when thick take off the fire, then add<lb/> a little Brandy when cool, some boil a<lb/> laurel leaf with cream sugar which such<lb/> improves the Custard.
