59<lb/> <head>Orange Marmalade</head><lb/> 12 bitter Seville oranges, 2 sweet + boil the peel<lb/> of the Seville oragnes 2 or 4 hours in 2 quarts of water<lb/> it well then be reduced to about 1 qurt, have<lb/> the water to settle for some hours, which you cut<lb/> the peels into the thinnest possible shapes, first<lb/> taking out all the white part which the peels<lb/> are boiling, scrape the pulp from the skins of<lb/> all the fruit (with a silver knife) + with the<lb/> juice add to the water + peels weight all toget<lb/> her + with the same weight of pounded sugar<lb/> boil 20 minutes<lb/> <head>Orange Preserve.</head><lb/> Take some of the best Seville Oranges at the begging<lb/> of April, + take off the rind of your Oranges, + put<lb/> them in a strong salt + water for 3 days, then<lb/> take them out + boil them in a bag, in a large<lb/> quantity of water till tender, then beat it<lb/> quite small in a Mortar, adding the pulp<lb/> + juice, when the pippins are taken out<lb/> then put them in a bottle, with double thee<lb/> weight of sugar (Loaf sugar) then let them boil<lb/> a four minutes till they will set in you pots.
