60<lb/> <head>- Green Gages -</head> <lb/> Take the largest Plumbs you can get, just before<lb/> they are ripe, put them into a pan, with a<lb/> layer of vine leaves at the bottom of your pan, then<lb/> a layer of Plumbs, do so till your pan is almost full<lb/> fill it with water set them on a slow fire, when<lb/> they are hot, take them off and take the skins<lb/> carefully off, put them on a sieve as you do them<lb/> then lay them in the same water with a layer<lb/> of leaves between, as you did at first, cover them very<lb/> close so that no steam can get out, + hange them a<lb/> great distance from the fire till they are green, which<lb/> will take 5. or 6. hours at least then take them up<lb/> + put them up in a good syrup give them a gentle<lb/> boil in it twice day for two days, take them out<lb/> + put them in a fine clear syrup, put paper dip-<lb/> -ped in Brandy over them, _ keep them for use.<lb/> <head>Apricot Preserve</head><lb/> Pair your apricots, + twist out the stones with a skewer<lb/> to every lt. of fruit, put 1 lb of Lump sugar strew part of it<lb/> over them, + let them stand 2 or 3 days, then give them a<lb/> boil gently 3. or 4 different times, let them stand till cold<lb/> each time, take them out of the syrup one by one
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

