63<lb/> sugar, fill up with Brandy + <unclear>the</unclear> a bladder over<lb/> <head>To preserve Siberian Crabs.</head><lb/> Make a good syrup, + when boiled quite clean, put<lb/> in the crabs, + boil them a short time + they will<lb/> soon be tender, take them out, + boil the syrup<lb/> + pour over them, do the same 2. or 3. times, a few<lb/> skins of Lemon boiled in the syrup give it an<lb/> agreeable flavor to a lt. of crabs put 3/4 lb. of Loaf sugar.<lb/> <head>To Keep Damsons.</head><lb/> To 1 lt. of Damsons, put 6 oz. of moist sugar, wet your<lb/> bladder + tie over them quite close, put them<lb/> into your water cold, let them boil 20 minutes<lb/> stand till they are cold in the water + keep<lb/> them in a dry place.<lb/> <head>To preserve Pears -</head> <lb/> Take 1 gallon of large pound pears + coddle them<lb/> well, then put them in cold water for a<lb/> little time, after which pare, core, + quarter them<lb/> make a syrup of 3 lbs. of Loaf sugar in 3 pints of<lb/> water, with the rinds of 3 Lemons pared very<lb/> thin, then cut in stripes, a very small quantity of<lb/> cochineal pounded + tied in a piece of muslin, then<lb/> put in the pears + let them boil till they are clear + ready<lb/> about an hour + a half will do them, when you take them<lb/> "off cold the juice of 3 Lemons."
