64<lb/> <head>Stew'd Pears or Apples.</head><lb/> Peel 6 large winter Pears, either quarter them<lb/> or do them whole, they make a pretty dish<lb/> with one whole, + the rest cut in quarters + the<lb/> core taken out, lay them in a deep earthen pot<lb/> with a few cloves, + a piece of Lemon peel, a <unclear>qill</unclear><lb/> of red wine, + a 1/4 of a lb. of Loaf sugar, if the pears<lb/> are very large, they will take 1/2 a lb. of sugar, +<lb/> half a pint of wine, cover them close with brown<lb/> paper, + bake them till they done enough.<lb/> <head>To Bottle Currants</head><lb/> Take 12 lbs. of red currants, put them into your pre<lb/> -serving bottle, with 3 lbs. of Loaf sugar, let them<lb/> simmer gently, for an hour have ready 6 quart<lb/> bottles, rinse them out with a little Brandy<lb/> + when your currants are cold, put them in<lb/> your bottles, + tie bladder over them.<lb/> "N. B." They will keep 2 years.<lb/> <head>To Bottle Gooseberries</head><lb/> Pick your walnut gooseberries, bottle them +<lb/> fill the bottles with spring water up to the<lb/> neck, cork them closely, the a bladder over +<lb/> set them in a dry place.
