80<lb/> the whole well lightly together, then strew in<lb/> Teaspoonful of good carbonate of Soda in<lb/> finest powder, + again beat the cake well &amp;<lb/> lightly, for 3 or 4 minutes, put it into a buttered<lb/> mould, bake it an hour and a quarter, or divide<lb/> it into into 2, when 3/4 of an hour will be sufficient<lb/> for each part.<lb/> <head>- Almond Cakes. -</head> <lb/> 2 ozs of butter, 6 oza. of sugar, 2 eggs, 2 ozs of Bitter<lb/> Almonds + 1 oz of sweet, + half pound of flour<lb/> <head>- A Rice Cake -</head> <lb/> 10 ozs. of ground rice, 8 ozs of powdered rice both to<lb/> be sifted through a hair sieve, the peel of a mid-<lb/> dled sized Lemon, sliced very small, 10 eggs only<lb/> 1/2 the whites, well beaten, then mix the rice<lb/> sugar + peel all together by degrees in an earthen<lb/> pan, + beat it for half an hour before you put it<lb/> in the oven, bake it 35 minutes. "Butter the Tin <hi rend="underline">well</hi>" <head>Another receipt for a Rice Cake</head><lb/> 1 Pint of new milk, 2 ozs. of ground rice, mix the rice<lb/> with part of theh milk cold, then add the re-<lb/> - mainder &amp; boil it 10 minutes stirring it all<lb/> the time, then put it into the mould after
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/085|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
81<lb/> <sic>sweetenging</sic> + flavouring it to your taste with<lb/> Lemon + cinnamon let it stand till cold<lb/> then turn it out, + pour a cold custard or<lb/> preserve round the dish.<lb/> <head>- Derbyshire Cakes. -</head> <lb/> 1 lb of flour, 1/2 lb. of butter, 1/2 lb. sugar, 2 ozs of currants<lb/> a few caraway seeds if approved + a small<lb/> teaspoonful of volatile salts.<lb/> <head>- Derbyshire Short Cakes. -</head> <lb/> Rub down 1 lb of butter into 2 lbs of flour, mix<lb/> with this 1/2 lb. of sifted sugar, an egg + as much<lb/> milk as will make a paste, roll it out there<lb/> + cut in any shapes you please, Bake them<lb/> on Tins about 10 minutes, they may be added<lb/> caraway seeds, + sifted sugar over them.<lb/> <head>- Lemon Biscuits. -</head> <lb/> Take 1 lb. of sugar sifted fine, 1 lb of flour, + 10 eggs<lb/> beat it an hour, + bake it in shallow tins.<lb/> <head>Sugar Tea Cakes.</head><lb/> Make a paste with 1 lb. of flour, 12 ozs. of sifted sugar the<lb/> yolks of 3 eggs, + a glass of <sic>oringe</sic> flower water roll it<lb/> out thin, cut it with a stamp on Glass strew<lb/> sugar over the cakes, + bake them.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/086|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
82<lb/> <head>- Lemon Biscuits. -</head> <lb/> Take 1 lb. of sugar sifted, + the rind of a Lemon<lb/> grated, mix them together with the white +<lb/> a half of an egg, bake them on tins.<lb/> <head>Breakfast Cakes -</head> <lb/> 1 1/2 lb. of flour, 1 egg, beat the yolk + white separate<lb/> -ly then malt 2 ozs. of butter, in two parts water<lb/> + one milk, mix them into a dough with 3 <lb/> spoonful of <sic>balm</sic>, + set it to the fire an hour to <add>rise</add>.<lb/> <head>Another receipt for Breakfast Cakes.</head><lb/> Take as much fine flour, as 1/2 a pint of cream will<lb/> make into dough, the white of 2 eggs the<lb/> yolk of one, 2 spoonful of yeast the cream sh-<lb/> -ould be a little warm, mix the whole to-<lb/> -gether, which will make 6. or 7. cakes. Let<lb/> them rise before the fire. They will bake in 10 minutes<lb/> <head>Brighton Cakes.</head><lb/> 3 1/2 lb.s of Dough, 3/4 lb. of Butter, 1 lb. currants four<lb/> eggs, 2 ozs. of caraway seeds 3/4 lb. of sugar first beat<lb/> the butter to a cream + warm the sugar<lb/> and currants before you put them in<lb/> together.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/087|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
83.<lb/> <head>- Shrewsbury Cakes. -</head> <lb/> Beat 1/2 lb. of cold butter to a cream, + mix with<lb/> it 6 ozs. of sifted sugar, 8 ozs. of flour a few caraway<lb/> seed + some pounded cinnamon, 2 eggs beat +<lb/> little Rose water. - Roll out the paste a quarter<lb/> of inch in thickness adding a little more flour<lb/> if necessary + stamp out the cakes any shape<lb/> or size you please<lb/> <head>A Fine Seed Cake</head><lb/> Take 1 1/2 lbs. of flour + 16 eggs well whisked, mix with<lb/> them 1 1/2 lb. of fine beat sugar + whisk them<lb/> well together - Put in 1/2 lb of cut candid peel<lb/> orange + citron, 4 ozs. of almonds blanched +<lb/> cut mix this with 1/2 lb of dried flour, + 12 oz. of<lb/> butter, beat to a cream, season with cinnamon<lb/> + cloves + thrown in a few caraway seeds.<lb/> <sic>Smoothe</sic> the <sic>tope</sic> of this (and every other cut of<lb/> cake) when put into the hoop.<lb/> <head>Ponder Cake</head><lb/> To 1 lb. of flour, 6 ozs. of sugar a dessert spoonful<lb/> of baking powder, 4 eggs 1/2 a pint of cream. Fruit<lb/> to your taste. - Mix the Powder in the flour<lb/> dry, + add the eggs + cream when ready for the<lb/> "<hi rend="underline">oven</hi>" _ _ _
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/088|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
84<lb/> <head>- Rock Cakes -</head> <lb/> 1 lb. of Flour, 2 lb. of Loaf sugar sifted 2 lb. butter<lb/> 1 egg + a few currants. - Drop them on Tins.<lb/> <head>Little Rough Cakes.</head><lb/> 1 lb. of flour, 1/2 lb. of butter, 6 ozs of loaf sugar, 3 eggs a<lb/> teaspoonful of volatile salts, 10 or 12 drops of<lb/> essence of Lemon.<lb/> <head>Spanish Cakes</head><lb/> 1 1/2 lb of fine flour, 6 ozs. of lump sugar, 5 eggs with<lb/> yolks + whites beat separately 1/2 lb of butter put<lb/> in when melted, + nearly cold, then add 1/2 lb<lb/> of currants + 2 ozs. candid peel, beat them together<lb/> &amp; drop in tins, or bake them in patty pans 20 minutes<lb/> <lb/> Rub 1 lb. butter very fine cut 1 lb. of fine flour<lb/> mix in it 1 lb. of loaf sugar, finely sifted + 2 ozs.<lb/> of caraway seeds pounded make it into an<lb/> paste with the white of 4 eggs, + roll it out<lb/> the thickness of your finger, + lay them on Tins.<lb/> in the shape of S. - Bake them in a cool oven<lb/> <head>Pound Cake</head><lb/> 1 lb. of butter, 1 lb. of currants, 1 lb. of sugar, 1 lb. of<lb/> flour, 12 eggs + part of the whites, beat the butter
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/089|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
85<lb/> to a cream, add the remainder + put it into<lb/> a <hi rend="underline">quick oven</hi>.<lb/> <head>Genoa Cakes.</head><lb/> Take 10 ozs. of flour, 8 ozs. of finely pounded loaf<lb/> sugar 8 ozs of butter beaten to a cream 4 eggs, 1<lb/> tablespoonful of brandy 1/2 lb of currants 1 Teaspoon<lb/> -ful of Carbonate of Ammonia. bake it in a<lb/> moderate oven.<lb/> <head>Lemon Cakes</head><lb/> Beat to a cream 1/4 lb. of butter, 1 lb. of flour, 6 ozs. of<lb/> lump sugar pounded fine, 4 <unclear>0</unclear> drops of essence of<lb/> Lemons, Moisten the whole with 2 eggs, Drop<lb/> in small lumps on a tin previous to dropping<lb/> them in pounded sugar.<lb/> <head>Another receipt for Lemon Cakes</head><lb/> Take 6 eggs, half the white, 1/2 lb. of sugar pounded<lb/> 1/4 lb. of flour, the rind of a Lemon grated mix<lb/> all <hi rend="underline">well</hi> together.<lb/> <head>- Queen Cakes. -</head> <lb/> Take 1 lb. of flour, 1 lb. butter, 1 lb. of sugar, 1 lb. of currants<lb/> 4 eggs leaving out 2 of the whites. "N. B." A little<lb/> Brandy as an improvement also a little<lb/> Lemon Peel.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/090|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
86<lb/> <head>Ginger Cakes. -</head> <lb/> 1 lb. of flour 1/2 lb of moist sugar 6 ozs. of Butter + 3/4 of<lb/> ozs. Ginger, mix together with 1 egg + a little<lb/> cream + wine.<lb/> <head>Ginger Bread</head><lb/> 1 lb. of flour, 1/2 lb. of butter, 1/2 lb. of sugar, 1/2 lb. of Treacle<lb/> 1/2 of oz. ginger, caraway seeds, + candid Peel to your taste.<lb/> <head>Small Cakes or Currant Cakes</head><lb/> 1 lb. of flour 1/2 lb of butter, 1/2 lb of Loaf sugar sifted<lb/> + 1/2 lb of currants 3 eggs, + a little candid Peel<lb/> 1/2 a glass of Brandy or White wine, - Bake them<lb/> on Tins of a light brown colour.<lb/> <head>Biscuits -</head> <lb/> 3 lbs of fine flour, 1/2 lb. of butter, 1/2 lb. of Lump sugar<lb/> 1 oz of Ammonia dissolved in a pint of new milk<lb/> just warm<lb/> <head>Hard Biscuits.</head><lb/> 1/4 lb. of butter, to 2 lbs of flour, mixed with cold milk<lb/> to a paste + moulded well at least an hour<lb/> make the biscuits up in round pieces<lb/> + press them in the middle very hard.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

