87<lb/> <head>To make <unclear>Whphroopis</unclear></head><lb/> 1/2 lb of sweet Almonds, 1/4 lb of bitter ones, beat them<lb/> as fine as possible, with the whites of 2 eggs, then<lb/> beat the whites of 5 eggs to a strong froth, shake<lb/> in lightly 1 1/2 of fine Loaf sugar, beat + sifted very<lb/> fine. - Drop them in little drops, the size of a <lb/> nutmeg, on case paper, + bake them in a slack oven<lb/> <head>Biscuits</head><lb/> 3/4 lb of flour, 1/2 lb of butter, 1/2 lb. of Lump sugar +<lb/> then yolks of two eggs.<lb/> <head>Scotch Bread.</head><lb/> 6 ozs. of four, 4 ozs. of butter, + 4 ozs. of sugar.<lb/> <head>Sponge Cakes.</head><lb/> 5 eggs, 1/2 lb. of Loaf sugar + beat all together for<lb/> 1/2 an hour, with a steel fork. - Previously take<lb/> the weight of 2 eggs, + a half of flour, then<lb/> grate in the rind of a Lemon, the juice may<lb/> be added at pleasure, stir in the flour + im-<lb/> -mediately pour it into a Tin, lined with butter<lb/> -ed paper, + let it instantly be put into <unclear>iathe</unclear> a c<gap/> <add><gap/></add><lb/> <head>Another Sponge Cake</head><lb/> Take 5 eggs, + the weight of 5 eggs in sifted sugar +<lb/> the weight of 3 in flour, beat the eggs + sugar 10 minutes
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/092|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
88<lb/> then add the flour beating it 20 minutes longer<lb/> Bake it 1/2 an hour in rather quick oven.<lb/> <head>- Biscuit Cake. -</head> <lb/> Take the yolks of 7 eggs, beat them well for 1/2 an<lb/> hour, add 3/4 lb. of Loaf sugar sifted very fine<lb/> beat the whites of the eggs to a strong froth +<lb/> mix them with the sugar + yolks, take 14 ozs.<lb/> of flour, dry it before the fire + sift it. Shake in<lb/> a few caraway seeds + a little grated Lemon<lb/> Peel, beat all well together, till it runs very<lb/> light, sift a little sugar over it, + bake it in<lb/> a quick oven about 3/4 of an hour.<lb/> <head>Another good Sponge Cake</head><lb/> Take the yolks of 6 eggs, + the white of 5 beat<lb/> separate for 1/2 an hour. 1/2 lb. of Loaf sugar sifted<lb/> fine, beat up with the eggs for 5 minutes<lb/> 7 ozs. of flour beat with them 5 minutes, + bake<lb/> it in a quick oven.<lb/> <head>Rusks.</head><lb/> Take 2 lbs. of flour rub into it 6 ozs. of butter, 6 ozs. of<lb/> Lump sugar sifted, a few caraway seeds +<lb/> 2 eggs to be mixed together with a little warm<lb/> milk, add 2 spoonful of yeast, let it stand
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

