89<lb/> 2 hours to rise, - Make it into rusks + cakes<lb/> bake them on tins.<lb/> <head>- To make Wig's -</head> <lb/> To a 1/4 of a stone of flour (fine) 10 ozs. of fine Loaf<lb/> sugar, 6 ozs. of Butter, 1/4 of a pint of yeast, 1 oz. of<lb/> Caraway seeds, 2 eggs, + 3 half pints of milk, the<lb/> whole mixed up together + stand 2 hours to<lb/> rise, then put on this, + cut an squares, but<lb/> not over with an egg. N. B. let them rise upon<lb/> tins before sent to the oven, the milk should<lb/> be warm, + the butter melted in it. Bake<lb/> 1/4 of an hour in a quick oven.<lb/> <head>Pound Cakes -</head> <lb/> 1 lb. of butter beaten to a cream, 1 lb. sifted loaf<lb/> sugar, 8 eggs, beaten 1 at a time, 1 lb. flour, <lb/> dried + sifted, 2 ozs. candid Lemon, + a few<lb/> caraway seeds, a few drops Essence of Lemon<lb/> a small quantity of Volatile Salts improves<lb/> it, bake in a mould well lined with pa-<lb/> -per - an hour will bake it in a moderate oven
