90.<lb/> <head>Tea Cakes</head><lb/> 2 lbs. of flour 3 Teaspoonful of Baking Powder<lb/> mixed well with the flour, 1/2 lb. of Butter and<lb/> a little moist sugar, 2 eggs beat and about 1/2 a<lb/> pint of cold milk, a little salt mix it well<lb/> together, + bake them directly. A few currants if agreeable.<lb/> <head>Wafer Biscuits</head><lb/> 1 lb of flour, 6 ozs. of butter, 4 ozs. of moist sugar mix<lb/> it up with cold milk, + well work it before<lb/> rolled out, prick them all over, and cut them<lb/> in shapes as thin as possible.<lb/> <head>A <hi rend="underline">good Currant Cake</hi>.</head><lb/> 1 lb of Butter, 1 lb. Currants,<lb/> 1 lb of Sugar, 1 1/2 lb. of Flour. 6 Eggs.<lb/> 1 Desertspoonful of Baking Powder<lb/> 1/2 Pint of warm Milk To mix it<lb/> bake in a hot Oven.
