130<lb/> <head>Miscellaneous Receipts.</head><lb/> <head>Circassian Cream-</head><lb/> 8 ozs. of lard (without Salt) 2 ozs. of Olive Oil 30 drops<lb/> of Cloves, 20 drops of Oil of Cassia. 2 drachms of<lb/> Palm Oil, 1/2 an oz. of White <unclear>Nase</unclear> 1/2 drachm of the<lb/> Essence of <unclear>Berqumot</unclear>. Melt the well lard and<lb/> oil together stir it until nearly cold then<lb/> add the perfume.<lb/> <head>Pomatum.</head><lb/> 1/4 lb. of Beef Marrow, 1/4 lb. of lard (without salt)<lb/> melt both together, strain through muslin<lb/> stir it until cool, then add 1/2 pint of Olive<lb/> Oil, + 1 oz. of Castor Oil, and as much Bergemotte<lb/> as will perfume it.<lb/> <head>Sip Salve</head><lb/> White was 2 1/2 <unclear>ranles</unclear>, spermaceti 1/4 of an ounce<lb/> Oil of Almonds 4 ounces. - Mix well together<lb/> and apply to the lips at night.<lb/> <head>Ointment for Chapped Hands.</head><lb/> 1/2 an ounce of Olive Oil, 1/4 of an ounce of Flouey<lb/> 1/4 of an ounce of Butter from the <unclear>churn</unclear>,<lb/> 1/4 of an ounce + 5 grams of White <unclear>nase</unclear>, To be well<lb/> mixed until nearly cold.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/135|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
131<lb/> <head>Receipt for Pills.</head><lb/> 1 oz. of Lemon Powder, 2 d. worth Steel Filings, 2 d. worth<lb/> saffron, 2 d. worth <unclear>bemia</unclear> Treacle, 1/4 lb. of Currants<lb/> to be well pounded and made into pills with<lb/> Rum._ And 3 to be taken night + morning.<lb/> <head>For Biles</head><lb/> Flancy mixed with moist sugar yellow soap<lb/> yolk of an egg, + fresh lard equal quantities<lb/> of each well mixed, spread on a piece of<lb/> very soft yellow leather, with a hole in<lb/> the centre of the plaster<lb/> <head>An excellent Receipt for Sprains</head><lb/> 1/4 pint of spirits of Turpentine + 1/2 pint of <hi rend="underline">old</hi><lb/> Ale, well shake the bottle before applying<lb/> to the affected Parts.<lb/> <head>An excellent receipt for Hooping Cough</head><lb/> 10 Grains of Cochineal <unclear>findy</unclear> powdered, 20 Grains Salt<lb/> of Tartar, put into 4 ozs. of cold water, + sweetened<lb/> with lump sugar. Give a child under one<lb/> year a dessert spoonful 4 times a day + the<lb/> same quantity of pearl barley Tea, directly after<lb/> A child 2 years olds or older, a full tablespoonful<lb/> 4 times a day ,+ the same quantity of pearl barley
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/136|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
133<lb/> Tea directly afterwards. - Apples scalded in<lb/> milk + the milk drained from them.<lb/> should be their chief food.<lb/> <head>Another receipt for Hooping Cough</head><lb/> Take 10 grains of Alum well pounded, mixed it<lb/> in a spoonful of water, which may be either<lb/> hot or cold, + a little sugar may or may not<lb/> be added. This Medicine to be taken every<lb/> morning, Noon, + night, After the first doses<lb/> increase the quantity amounts to 20 grains<lb/> 3 times a day, which must be continued until<lb/> the cough is removed, which is generally in<lb/> a very few days. The dozes mentioned her are<lb/> for children about 14, adults may increase<lb/> the quantity to 26 grams- Infants may begin<lb/> with 4 or 5 grains + increase 2 grains each<lb/> time until the quantity amounts to 14 or 15<lb/> grains, &amp; continue that quantity until the<lb/> cough is removed<lb/> Observe no other medicine must be given at the<lb/> same time. If aperients should appear to be<lb/> required, at first they must not be given, as<lb/> the increasing doses of Alum will remove
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/005/001/137|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
133.<lb/> the necessity. This Medicine may be<lb/> given in any stage of the disease, but<lb/> <hi rend="underline">milk must</hi> not be given as food. Wine &amp;<lb/> Beer should be avoided, but as much good<lb/> Broth may be given as they like. The<lb/> best hours for taking are in the morning<lb/> or 1/2 an hour before breakfast, 12 at noon, +<lb/> 4 in the afternoon. - At 8 years of age be-<lb/> -gin with 8 grains &amp; increase to 16 grains<lb/> to 14 grains three times a day.<lb/> <head>For a Cough No 1</head><lb/> Take a new laid Egg, squeeze the juice of 2<lb/> lemons over it, &amp; let it stand till the Egg<lb/> is dissolved, then add 1 oz. of Spanish juice<lb/> 1 oz. of Sugar Candy, 1 oz. of Honey, &amp; 1/4 of a pint<lb/> of Rum. "N. B." You must not break the<lb/> Egg the shell will dissolve.<lb/> <head>Cough N2</head><lb/> 20 Grains of <unclear>Spicaenana</unclear> 40 drops of Laudanum<lb/> 1/4 lb. of Honey clarified in 1/2 a Teaspoonful of vin-<lb/> egar. Put all into a 1/2 pint bottle + fill it<lb/> up with water. Take 2 or 3 Tablespoonful 2 or 3<lb/> times a day.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

