135.<lb/> neck for 10 minutes in cold weather before<lb/> the fire at bedtime, bind it up with an<lb/> handkerchief &amp; wash it off in the morning<lb/> with warm water.<lb/> <head>Receipt for Chilblains</head><lb/> 3 Eggs well beat &amp; mixed with 1/2 a pint<lb/> of Turpentine &amp; 1/2 a pint of vinegar.<lb/> Shake it well, before applying every night.<lb/> <head>A Cure for Rheumatism</head><lb/> Opodelderk Camphorated Oil, Spirit of<lb/> Turpentine, Laudanum of each 1 oz. To<lb/> be mixed together &amp; the affected points to<lb/> be well rubbed there with night + morning<lb/> <head>For Cuts. Bruises &amp; Burns</head><lb/> 1 oz. of Hartshorn, 1 oz. of <unclear>Apodildock</unclear>, 2 ozs. of<lb/> Spirits of Wine, 2 ozs. of Oil of Camphor, + 2<lb/> drachms of Oil of <unclear>Oriquim</unclear>.<lb/> <head>To make Linseed Tea</head><lb/> 1/4 lb of linseed 1/4 lb of liquorish root, 1/4 lb. of<lb/> rasins, boiled in 2 quarts of water till<lb/> reduced to 1 quart, then add the juice<lb/> of a lemon, &amp; a 1/4 lb. of sugar candy when<lb/> for a cough.
