136.<lb/> <head>To remove Grease from Cloth. Silk &amp;c</head><lb/> 1 Pennyworth of Ammonia to 1 pint of<lb/> water &amp; keep it boiling hot while using<lb/> it, &amp; you will find it removes all grease<lb/> &amp; restores the colour.<lb/> <head>To Clean Silk</head><lb/> 1/4 lb. of white soap 1/4 lb. of Honey 1 quart<lb/> of soft water, 1 pint of gin dissolved<lb/> together, well brush the silk with,<lb/> it and rinse it in 2 or 3 cold waters.<lb/> Hang it to drain then <unclear>cron</unclear> it.<lb/> <head><sic>Furiture</sic> Cream</head><lb/> 1/2 pint of Turpentine, 1/2 a pint of red<lb/> furniture Oil, 1 oz. of bees wax, set it to the<lb/> fire till melted, then add 1/2 a pint<lb/> of vinegar, while it is warm, if it is too<lb/> thick, add a little more vinegar.<lb/> <head>French Polish Receipt</head><lb/> To 1 pint of spirits of Wine, 2 ozs. of gum<lb/> Shilaen, 1 oz. of gum <unclear>Scadlace</unclear>, 1 oz. of gum<lb/> Sandrake dissolved in a jar by the<lb/> slow fire 20 minutes. Then it is fit for use.
