To make Paint which answers for outdoor<add>ut</add><lb/> work<lb/> Dip 8 ounces of Lime in water &amp; expose it to the<lb/> air, when slaked mix it with a pint of skimmd<lb/> milk, then add by slow degrees six ounces of<lb/> Linseed oil, in which 2 ounces of white Burgun<lb/> dy Pith has been dissolved before over a<lb/> slow fire. &amp; when these several ingredients<lb/> are thoroughly blended, then mix with this<lb/> three pints more milk, &amp; three pounds of<lb/> Spanish white - this composition will be<lb/> fit to use in two Days. - 2 Coats of this<lb/> is sufficient &amp; this quantity is sufficient<lb/> for 2y. square yards of wood --<lb/> of 2y
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

