4<lb/> <hi rend="underline">To Make Gibblet Soup</hi><lb/> Stew the Giblets till they are all to pieces, add<lb/> a little Bit of Beef, Mutton, or Veal, an Onion<lb/> Stuck with Cloves, a little Jamaica or Black<lb/> Pepper, when stew'd enough take the Meat out<lb/> + Giblets, + strain it take some Butter + brown<lb/> it with flour to make the soup as thick as a<lb/> rich cream, add if wanted more Pepper, +<lb/> Salt + a Tea cup full of white wine, boil<lb/> it, + scum it, then add the Giblets, put a little<lb/> green onion, + parsley chopt small. then send<lb/> it to Table.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Whole Rice Pudding-</hi><lb/> Take a Tea Cup full of whole Rice wash + pick<lb/> it clean, set it over the fire, + let the Rice burst<lb/> with a little water, then put in some milk + let it<lb/> boil till tender take care to have the rice very<lb/> thick, add three large spoonfulls of Sugar<lb/> two Eggs beaten, + some nutmeg- butter a Bason<lb/> + put it in boil it three quarters of an Hour.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

