5<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Apple Pudding-</hi><lb/> The pulp of a sufficient quantity of apples to make<lb/> a pint when Boiled, as for apple sauce, put in 2 oz.<lb/> of Butter, a little Lemon Peel, sweeten it to your<lb/> taste; when cold, stir in the yolks of 6 Eggs put it<lb/> into a crust to bake. 1/4 of an Hour will bake it<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Apples Preserved Whole.</hi><lb/> Boil some fine Sugar in water + skim it well<lb/> pare your golden Pippins thin, Core them + put them<lb/> to the Sy<add>r</add>rup + let it Simmer till they are tender<lb/> put in the juice of a Lemon and some Peel shre'd<unclear>fu</unclear><lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Egg Mince Pies</hi><lb/> Take 1 lb of hard Eggs two lb 1/2 of Suet 1/2 of Currants<lb/> 1/2 lb of Sugar, 6 or 7 blades of mace 1/2 oz of Cinnamon<lb/> 1 large Nutmeg grate in some Lemon peel 2<lb/> glasses of white wine 1/2 lb. of stoned raisins chopped<lb/> fine, if you like it put in some citron orange +<lb/> Lemon Peel.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

