6<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Partridge Soup.</hi><lb/> Two Brace of Partridges + a serag of Veal to <lb/> 4 quarts of Water, a few sweet Herbs a blade<lb/> or two of Mace some Pepper kernels, a small<lb/> Onion, let it boil gently for two Hours then strain<lb/> it and put it into a Saucepan, with it two Heads<lb/> of Celery two of Lettuce two small onions two<lb/> oz of Rice one of Vermicella let this boil on<lb/> Hour, then put a pint of Cream + let it boil<lb/> after the cream is put to it care must be taken<lb/> it does not curdle.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">White Soup.</hi><lb/> Take a knuckle of Veal, a serag of Mutton<lb/> Boiled well in water enough to cover them <del>some</del><lb/> with some Onions, pepper &amp; salt to your <sic>tast</sic> skim<lb/> it + let it settle then pour off the fine part when <lb/> cold take off the fat, Blanch 1/4 of a lb. of sweet<lb/> Almonds in hot water then put them into cold<lb/> pound them very fine with a little Veal or Mutton<lb/> gravy take the Breast of a Chicken or a small piece
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

