7<lb/> of Veal pound it with the almonds + 4 Eggs boild<lb/> hard, boil the crumb of a French Koll in a pint<lb/> of good cream, then mix with it the almonds +<lb/> eggs put the soup to it, <del>put</del> + Rub them hard thro<lb/> a fine sieve Boil it very gently + skim it let it<lb/> Boil till <hi rend="underline">all</hi> the Skim is off salt must be added<lb/> to your taste.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Spice Cake-</hi><lb/> To a Pound of Flour put 1/2 lb of Sugar, 1/4 an<lb/> oz of Ginger and 24 Cloves beat fine, grate it<lb/> 1/2 the Peel of a Lemon, mix all them together +<lb/> then melt 1/2 a lb Butter in 1/4 lb Treacle pour<lb/> it to the Flour and beat it well, let it lay 1/2 <lb/> an Hour to rise, and it is ready to bake in<lb/> what form you please.<lb/> <hi rend="underline">White Sauce.</hi><lb/> Take a little Cream + a little white gravy a<lb/> little flour a piece of Butter pepper Salt<lb/> + Nutmeg, a little Lemon Peel + the juice a<lb/> Shalot + some Mushrooms about <hi rend="underline">half the</hi><lb/> yolk of an Egg.
