8<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Simolina Pudding</hi> <lb/> To two oz of Simolina, one pint of new milk, boil'd<lb/> till as thick as Custard, stirring it all the time<lb/> when a little cool put in a piece of Butter the<lb/> size of a large Walnut an oz + 1/2 of Loaf Sugar<lb/> the rind of 1/2 a Lemon grated when quite cold add<lb/> two Eggs and if liked, wine, almonds, + sweet-<lb/> = meats. It is good boiled or Baked.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">German Puffs.</hi><lb/> Take the yolks of 4 Eggs mix in three spoonfuls<lb/> of Flour, a pint of Cream, 2 oz of almonds blanched<lb/> + beaten fine a little clarified Butter sweeten it<lb/> to your taste put it into Cases + bake them.-<lb/> Scalt Pudding<lb/> A Pint of new milk scalding hot put to four<lb/> spoonfulls of Flour cover it down close + cut it<lb/> stand till it is just cold then braid it well<lb/> with a spoon till you break the lumps then put in<lb/> 6 Eggs leave out three whites, 1/4 of an Hour will bake or<lb/> boil it. your same wine + Butter.
