9<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Mince Pies.-</hi><lb/> To every pound of Meat two pounds of Suet two of<lb/> Currants, one pound of Raisins when stoned<lb/> Mace, Nutmeg, + <add>Cinnamon</add> <del>onions</del> of each 3/3 of an oz,<lb/> Salt to your taste, the Peel + juice of a Lemon<lb/> 1/2 a Pound of Sugar, plenty of chopt apple,<lb/> a Glass of Brandy 3/4 of a pint of white wine the<lb/> meat should be boiled till you can pull it to<lb/> Pieces or it will decay.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Apricot Marmalade.</hi><lb/> Weigh your apricots + take half the weight of<lb/> Loaf Sugar grated, stone, pare + cut them in thin<lb/> slices put a layer of sugar + a layer of apricot<lb/> into a Bason till they are all in let them strain<lb/> a night close cover'd, the next morning set<lb/> them over a charcole fire boiling slow till they<lb/> are a marmalade keep stirring them all the<lb/> time <unclear>clse</unclear> they will Burn skim it as it rises.
