10<lb/> <hi rend="underline">French Dumpling.-</hi><lb/> To a penny Loaf grated put half a lb. of Currants<lb/> three quarter of a lb Beef suet shred fine half a<lb/> nutmeg some sugar the yolks of three Eggs three<lb/> spoonfulls of white wine + the same quantity of<lb/> cream, mix the Ingredients together, make it<lb/> the size of a large apple, tie them up in cloth<lb/> put them into boiling water + let them boil three<lb/> quarters of an hour. - Sweet sauce in the dish.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Empress of Russias Soup.</hi><lb/> Six quarts of Water three lb lean Beef 1/4 of lb.<lb/> Flour Rice, 2 large Potatoes 2 Onion, + one Turnip<lb/> pepper + Salt to your tast, boil it to one Gallon<lb/> strain it thro' a Cullunder then thro' a Sieve<lb/> heat it, serve it up with a piece of Butter the<lb/> size of a Walnut + a French Roll.<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Currant Wine.</hi><lb/> Boil clear spring Water, let it stand till<lb/> cold, the Currants Brusied or strain'd thro' a <lb/> Cloth, pick out all bad ones Red or White Currants<lb/> will do, to 2 quarts of juice put 2 quarts of Water
