14<lb/> every other day for a fortnight + let them stand<lb/> in the <unclear>chrinneg</unclear> corner all the time + they will<lb/> soon look Gren you may put small <sic>Gurkins</sic><lb/> into your large ones if you like it.<lb/> <pb/> To preserve ripe Melon<lb/> Cut the Melon in quarters lay it in water 2 Days<lb/> take it out + wipe it dry, then scaled it in clean <lb/> water; make a Syrup of one lb: of sugar to half<lb/> a pint of water, boil it well + skim it till all<lb/> the Drops is gone; then put in the Melon with<lb/> some grated Ginger, + Lemon Peel shred fine<lb/> scald the Syrup three Days, taking out the Melon<lb/> + putting it in again when the Syrup is cold, or<lb/> it will make the melon too soft if it is put<lb/> in hot. you must allow a pound + half of sugar<lb/> to one lb. of Melon. - Green Melon or cucumber<lb/> are good done the same way.
