17<lb/> Dried Fruit Cakes<lb/> Put the Fruit into an Earthen Pot, set it in a slow<lb/> oven till baked quite soft, strain, + braid the Juice<lb/> Pulp thro' a fine Cullender, + to every Pint of this<lb/> put a pound of Sugar roll'd + sifted. &amp; the White<lb/> of one Egg. beat + mix it well together. put it in<lb/> moulds + dry them in a slow oven.<lb/> <pb/> Artificial yeast.-<lb/> Boil Potatoes of the Mealy sort till they are<lb/> thoroughly tender, skim + braid them smooth,<lb/> put as much warm Water as will make it as thick<lb/> as common Beer yeast, but not thicker. add to<lb/> every pound of Potatoes, 2 ounces of coarse Sugar<lb/> + whilst Just warm put to it a quarter of a<lb/> pint of good new yeast. strain it all thro' a Cullinder<lb/> set it before the Fire to work + when the ferment<lb/> -ation is over set it by for use. the bread made
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

