18<lb/> of this yeast must be made very stiff, + lay 8<lb/> Hours before the Fire to rise. when it will be<lb/> very good. - This yeast will keep a month good.<lb/> <pb/> To make Catchup of Walnuts. for Fish Sauce<lb/> Take young Walnuts. bruise them, put a Handfull<lb/> of Salt to them, let them stand all night, strain<lb/> them thro' a fine Hair Sieve, + to every Gallon of<lb/> this Liquor add half a pound of anchovies &amp; some<lb/> long Pepper, + black Pepper. when cold strain it<lb/> again, + bottle it for use<lb/> <pb/> Potatoe Pudding.-<lb/> Boil a doz<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">n</hi> Potatoes till they are quite tender, peel them<lb/> &amp; whilst they are hot braid them with six ounces of<lb/> Butter, sweeten it to your taste, let it stand till cool<lb/> &amp; add the yolks of 6 Eggs, + the whites of three. grate<lb/> in a little nutmeg, &amp; a little Bread. add a spoonful<lb/> of orange Brandy. put it into a Puff Paste at<lb/> the Bottom of the Baking Dish. bake it an<lb/> Hour.-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/006/001/026|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
19<lb/> To make Cream Flummery. -<lb/> Take a Pint of Cream, a quarter of an oz of Isinglass<lb/> three spoonfuls of ground Rice, three oz of Sugar, 2<lb/> oz of almonds blanch'd, + beaten fine in a mortar,<lb/> (with a little milk to keep them from oiling) &amp; the<lb/> whites of three Eggs well beaten. strain the Eggs, mix<lb/> them carefully with the Cream, Rice, Almonds, &amp; Sugar<lb/> set them over a slow Fire, stirring it all the time<lb/> till it be thick &amp; smooth as custard, keep it<lb/> stirring till almost cold, then put it into moulds<lb/> dipped in cold water. - you may prick. it with<lb/> almonds sliced thin to send it to Table when<lb/> turned out of the moulds.<lb/> <pb/> Apricot Cream.<lb/> Dissolve half an Ounce of Isinglass in a quart of Cream<lb/> over a very slow Firre. sweeten it, + Graid in sufficient<lb/> apricot marmalade to make it taste. stir it till<lb/> nearly cold, put in a Glass Dish, &amp; ornament it with<lb/> little marmalade laid on the Top. <hi rend="underline">in small</hi> pieces
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/006/001/027|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
20<lb/> Stewed Onions<lb/> Put some middle sized onions, stew them till tender<lb/> with a little Pepper + Salt, thick the liquor with<lb/> a Piece of Butter braided in Flour, + brown the<lb/> Gravy with a <add>little</add> burnt sugar. Toast some bread very<lb/> thin, + pour it over the Toast to eat with the Onions.<lb/> <pb/> To make Ox Turtle Soup.-<lb/> clean an Ox Cheek wile with Cold water, + then<lb/> with warm. - Cut it into square Pieces from the<lb/> Bone. put in some Pepper, &amp; Salt, a little Lemon<lb/> Thyme, Lemon Peel, &amp; Onions cuts small, Put it<lb/> into a Stew Pan with a Gallon of Water stew it<lb/> half away, then add a pint of Lisbon or Sherry<lb/> Skim off all the Fat with care, braid a piece<lb/> of Butter in Flour + when the Soup has stewed<lb/> after the wine in some little Time, thicken it<lb/> with this, + the yolk of 2 Eggs boil'd hard +<lb/> braided with a little Cayenne Pepper, + a little<lb/> Lemon Pickle. serve up the soup, with the meat, + hard Eggs.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/006/001/028|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
21<lb/> To make Cheese Cakes -<lb/> Take half a pint of cheese Curd, + a quarter of<lb/> a pound of Sugar, Beat it well, add to it the yolk<lb/> of four Eggs + the white of two well beaten. - <lb/> a quarter of a pound of currants wash'd + pick'd<lb/> + plump'd in Brandy, + a few almonds blanch'd<lb/> + shred very fine. - Mix these well together +<lb/> bake them in a good puff Paste. - <lb/> <pb/> Hartshorn Jelly<lb/> Take two ounces of Hartshorn Shavings, half<lb/> an ounce of Isinglass, + one quart of water, <lb/> let these be well boil'd. then add a quarter<lb/> of a lb of Sugar. a pint of white wine, the<lb/> Juice of two Lemons, + the peel of one, the<lb/> whites of five Eggs well beaten. - let these boil<lb/> again for a quarter of an Hour, + then <unclear>fine</unclear><lb/> it thro' a Jelly Bag. - it must be pass'd thro'<lb/> the Bag till quite clear. -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/006/001/029|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
22<lb/> To make a Lemon or Orange<lb/> Puddings, or Cheese Cakes. - <lb/> Boil the thick Peels of three Lemons or<lb/> Seville Oranges in three waters till quite<lb/> tender, the Oranges will require more<lb/> water than the Lemons because they<lb/> are bitterer.- then beat them well in a<lb/> marble mortar, with three quarters of a<lb/> pound of Loaf Sugar, + a quarter of a<lb/> pound of almonds blanch'ed. - then<lb/> add half a pound of Butter, the yolks<lb/> of 8 Eggs. + the whites of 2.- put it into<lb/> Puff Paste, + bake it either as Pudding or<lb/> CheeseCakes. - the Lemons will boil in 2 Hours<lb/> the Oranges 2 Hours<pb/>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

