17<lb/> To make Madera Wine M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <unclear>Rixon</unclear><lb/> To every gallon of water, put one quart of ale <unclear>wart</unclear><lb/> taken out of the vat while working, 3 pounds of<lb/> moist sugar to every gallon of this liquor, 2 pounds<lb/> of raisins to 18 gallons of wine 2 ounces of isin<lb/> glass and 1/2 a pound of sugar candy and one bottle<lb/> of brandy, boil the water and sugar, half an hour<lb/> put the ale to it when cold and the other ingredients<lb/> when done fermenting<lb/> <pb/> To make Sherry Wine. M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <unclear>Rixon</unclear><lb/> To 3 pounds of moist sugar, put 2 quarts of<lb/> water well boiled and skimmed, when cool add<lb/> to every gallon 1 quart of ale moist, and when<lb/> <unclear>tinned</unclear> put one pound of raisins to every gallon<lb/> with a little isinglass<lb/> <pb/> Grape Wine - Hereford<lb/> five pints of the juice of Grapes to a Gallon of<lb/> Water, add three pounds of sugar thro the<lb/> Skins into water + let them lay all night squeeze<lb/> them thro' a Hair Sieve, then measure the water<lb/> + put it to the Grapes, by which means you <unclear>will</unclear><lb/> all the goodness out of the Grapes - when tunn'd a<lb/> short time add to every Gallon of Wine a 1/4 pint of<lb/> Brandy. <unclear>Guns</unclear> it. Down + let it stand a year before bottle
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

