68<lb/> Puff Paste Hereford<lb/> To one pound of Flour take a 1/4 of a pound of Butter<lb/> rub it quite fine in the flour, Take the white of<lb/> an Egg, beat it well with sufficient water to wet<lb/> the Paste, + make it pretty moist, then roll it<lb/> out as broad as you can, take half a lb <unclear>more</unclear><lb/> butter, + stick it with a fourth part in small<lb/> pieces all over your Paste, then roll it up but<lb/> do not knead it with your Hands, do this four<lb/> times till all the Butter is in, dredging Flour.<lb/> very thick over each time before you roll it<lb/> up, with some of the same Flour, which you must<lb/> reserve for that purpose. - <lb/> <pb/> Short Crust - Hereford.<lb/> To every pound of Flour put half a pound of butter <lb/> rub a small quantity into the F<add>l</add>our with a <lb/> little loaf sugar sifted fine melt the remainder <lb/> of the butter in hot water + skim it off as fast <lb/> as soon as possible but do not make it too <unclear>fast</unclear> <lb/> roll it out and put it over your Fruit. <pb/>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

