70<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Substitute for Soap</hi> Hereford<lb/> Peel off the rind of the Horn Chesnut + grind<lb/> them the meal of 20 large nuts is sufficient<lb/> for <del>11</del> 10 quarts of Water either Linnen or<lb/> Wools may be washed in the infusion with<lb/> out any kind of soap it takes out spots<lb/> rincing the linnen well in clear water the<lb/> same Meal steep'd in Hot Water + mix'd in<lb/> with <del>some</del> an equal quantity of Bran makes<lb/> a good Food for Hag or Poultry. - <lb/> <pb/> 44 To bottle Damsons Hereford<lb/> put them into bottle well dried, first<lb/> pricking every Damson with a needle they<lb/> must not be too ripe, cork the bottles<lb/> very tight, cut the corks close, then lye<lb/> them down with a Bladder, soak'd in water<lb/> set them in the oven after the Bread<lb/> is drawn, when quite enough keep them<lb/> in a dry place, they will keep good 2 y<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <pb/>
