73<lb/> Cream Cheese M<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Hereford<lb/> Take a bit of Calves maw, the size of a shilling<lb/> steep it in a tea Cup full of warm milk + water<lb/> five Hours. then put it into six quarts of new milk<lb/> warm from the Cow, to which add one pint of sweet<lb/> Cream. - when sufficiently run, lay a Cheese Cloth,<lb/> into the vat, which ought to be two inches deep, +<lb/> to measure round one foot + half. take up the<lb/> Curd lightly with a Skimmer, or fleeting Dish<lb/> put it into the Vat, the next Day press it<lb/> with a pound Weight. - + let it remain till<lb/> sufficiently press'd which must not be much<lb/> after it is taken out of the vat it must be<lb/> kept <add>in</add> a wet Cloth till it be ripe, changing<lb/> the cloth every Day.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

