74<lb/> Fruit in Jelly. - M<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Hereford<lb/> put a pint of Calves Foot Jelly when made + clear'd<lb/> fit for Table into a Bason, + when it is cool'd + <lb/> stiffened lay in three Peaches. + a fine bunch of<lb/> Grapes. with the stalks upwards, + a few Vine<lb/> Leaves over them. then fill up the Bowl with<lb/> Jelly; let it stand till the next Day. -<lb/> when you want to send it to Table set the<lb/> Bason nearly to the Brim into warm Water,<lb/> + as soon as the Jelly losens from the Bason<lb/> take it out, + turn it out upon a Dish +<lb/> serve it to Table. -<lb/> To make Gum Paste for Desert Baskets + <add>covers</add><lb/> Steep one ounce of Gum Dragon in a Cup of cold water<lb/> all night, then have ready one pound of double refin'd<lb/> Sugar sifted through a tiffany Sieve, then mix the Gum<lb/> + sugar together with a strong Hand. + in working<lb/> it will become as white as snow, then with a little<lb/> fine Hair powder make it into a stiff Paste<lb/> and cut it into any figure you please dry it in a<lb/> very cool Oven, + it is fit for use in Deserts +c.
