75<lb/> To Pickle Walnuts black.<lb/> Gather walnuts when so soft you can<lb/> pierce a Pin thro' them. lay them in a strong<lb/> brine of salt + water for 9 Days, + change<lb/> the water every three Days stirring them twice<lb/> a Day, put them in a Hair Sieve till they turn<lb/> dark, then put them into Pickle Jars, + pour <lb/> boiling Vinegar over them, cover them + let them<lb/> stand till cold. then boil the vinegar three<lb/> times more, standing till cold betwixt each<lb/> boiling. - tye them down close, + let them<lb/> stand two months. - then make a strong pickle<lb/> + to every quart of Vinegar put 1/2 an oz of<lb/> Cloves, Ginger + long Pepper, + 2 ounces of<lb/> common Salt. boil this a quarter of an<lb/> Hour, + pour it hot over the walnuts. tye<lb/> them down with a Bladder moisten'd, +<lb/> then a paper over it. - they will be<lb/> then fit for use
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

