79<lb/> same manner on very good, adding<lb/> to the latter a little beaten pepper, with<lb/> the Salt Peter; smooth Dry them a little.<lb/> <pb/> Gravy Soup M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <hi rend="underline">Roker Tw<gap/></hi><lb/> Take a Skin of 4 lb<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">s</hi> of the <unclear>ruck</unclear> of <unclear>Bay</unclear><lb/> put it in a Saucepan, with 1/2 a pint of<lb/> water, 6 onions, 4 heads 2 Turnips<lb/> a Carrot, 12 grains of Allspice. <hi rend="underline">sweat</hi> <lb/> it till it sticks, then pour 4 quarts of <lb/> boiling water on it, when it boil scum<lb/> it well, + stew it gently till half the <unclear>lign<gap/></unclear><lb/> is water - <unclear>scawn</unclear> it, strain it, put it by<lb/> till cold <add>to</add> take off all the fat. - then<lb/> it ought to be made the day before use<lb/> then add Carrots, turnip, celery, + white<lb/> Beet leaves cut small, also a little<lb/> <unclear>Mouarim</unclear>, or Vermicelli, but the first<lb/> is best for gravy soup, + the latter for<lb/> White soup. -
