81<lb/> Rice Cake<lb/> To 6 ounces of pound rice, put 6 oz<hi rend="underline">s</hi> of flour<lb/> 14 Oz of sugar, and 6 eggs- beat it an hour<lb/> it will require an hour to bake it -<lb/> Gingerbread<lb/> Four pounds of flour, 2 lb treacle, 1 1/2 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">lb</hi> of butter<lb/> 1 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">lb</hi> sugar, 3 1/2 Oz<hi rend="underline">s</hi> Ginger, 5 dozen cloves, 5 Oz<hi rend="underline">s</hi><lb/> candied peel, and some lemon peel - <lb/> Preserv'd Barberries<lb/> Boil powder'd lump sugar to a syrup, then<lb/> put Barberries in till they are but just covered<lb/> with the syrup. boil them ten minutes, + put<lb/> them into jars- <lb/> A Hunting Pudding<lb/> <add><unclear>Raspe</unclear></add><unclear>Bre</unclear> poured of beef suet, 1 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">lb</hi> Raisins ston'd<lb/> 5 eggs, leave out 4 whites, 4 spoonful of flour<lb/> 4 of sugar, + 2 of Brandy, a little nutmeg<lb/> salt - it will take four hours to boil<lb/> To Collar Eels<lb/> Take out the bones, lay them in a cloth<lb/> when dry season them with pepper, salt, mace<lb/> and cloves, roll them as hard as you possible
