82<lb/> can, + bind them with a <unclear>broid</unclear> Tape, boil<lb/> them in water with a small quantity of<lb/> vinegar + the bones of the fish. when they<lb/> have boil'd 1/2 and hour, take them out, when<lb/> quite cold, put them to the liquor + tie<lb/> them up -<lb/> Potted Beef - <lb/> Put 1 1/2 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">lb</hi> of lean Beef in slices put to it 1/2<lb/> ounce of salt petre, let it lay in a dish<lb/> 24 hours, take it out + put it in a pan<lb/> with water, a little butter + salt, tie it<lb/> over with wetted paper, let it stand in the<lb/> oven all night, in the morning take it out<lb/> beat it in a marble mortar with 1/2 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">pt</hi> of <unclear>bath</unclear><lb/> till it is a paste, season it with mace<lb/> pepper, + salt to your taste, press it hard<lb/> in a pan, pour oil'd butter over it -<lb/> To stew Spinage<lb/> Stew the spinage sometime in a saucepan,<lb/> then put it into a frying pan with butter, +<lb/> the juice of a Lemon, keep stirring it all<lb/> the time, when enough put it on a white bread toast
