83<lb/> Artificial Brown.<lb/> Boil the pigs feet, ears + eye pieces till the <lb/> bones will slaw out, preserve the skin as well<lb/> you can, lay some of it at the bottom of <gap/><lb/> vat, chop the meat as fast as you can when<lb/> it is hot season it with pepper, salt, mace, and <gap/><lb/> or 3 cloves, put it hot into the vat, lay the w<gap/><lb/> =der of the skin over it, and press it - when it has<lb/> been a sufficient time in the press take it out<lb/> put it into a deep pan, cover it with the liquor<lb/> it was boil'd in, with the addition of some salt<lb/> and vinegar, - it is the best pickle for its preserve<lb/> Trifle-<lb/> Lay Macaroons in white wine at the bottom of <lb/> a glass dish, put a very thick custard over<lb/> stick slices of candied peel in it, fill it with<lb/> <sic>sillabub</sic> + froth it very high - <lb/> Raspberry Vinegar<lb/> Put some rasberries into a pot, with as much<lb/> vinegar as will cover them, let them stand 9<lb/> days, strain off the juice, to every fruit part<lb/> 3/4 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">lb</hi> lump sugar, boil it 15 minutes, when cold<lb/> bottle it for use Black Currant is made the same
