M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Robertson -<lb/> a good common plumb Cake<lb/> Rub 6 ounces of Butter into one pound of<lb/> Flour, grate in a little nutmeg; beat well<lb/> 2 Eggs, + strain them. put to them a tea cup<lb/> full of good Barm, + as much warm milk<lb/> as will make it into a Dough, then set it<lb/> to the Fire to rise. - have ready half a<lb/> pound of Currants well wash'd, + dried. +<lb/> a quarter of a pound of Sugar- work this<lb/> well together, + then put it into the Oven<lb/> + bake it an Hour. - <lb/> Sago Pudding<lb/> Wash 2 oz of Sago in three waters, then boil<lb/> it in a pint of milk till tender, set it by<lb/> till cool. then add five Eggs, 2 Naples<lb/> Biscuits a small glass of Brandy - sugar to<lb/> your Taste- butter a Bason + boil it in<lb/> it an Hour - serve it to Table with<lb/> melted Butter with a Wine Glass full of Wine<lb/> + sugar to your taste. -
