Cowslip Wine<lb/> To six Gallons of water put 18 pounds of Sugar<lb/> the Juice of 6 Lemons, <add>+ 4 oz of Ginger</add> the whites of four Eggs<lb/> well beaten; boil them half an Hour skim it<lb/> well. take one peel of Cowslips pick'd, or if the<lb/> blossoms be dried half a peck will do- put them<lb/> into a Tub with the thin <unclear>pariays</unclear> of the Lemons<lb/> + pour the liquor on them quite hot stir them<lb/> well. + when almost cold put in a thin Toast<lb/> spread with yeast, + let it stand to work<lb/> two Days. - and oz of Syrrup of Citron, or Lemons<lb/> will greatly improve it. + a pint of Brandy<lb/> to this quantity when you turn it. - Squeeze<lb/> the cowslips thro' a corse strainer before you<lb/> tun the liquor. - lay the Bung close a few<lb/> Days + then bung it tight down - it will be<lb/> fit to Bottle in three months.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

