To pot Mackarel - Miss Rye<lb/> To wine Mackarel well clean'd + dried<lb/> put on oz of ground pepper - 1/4 of an Oz of<lb/> nutmegs. 1/4 of an oz whole pepper 1/2 an oz of<lb/> Ginger sliced. - cut off the Heads + tails <del>of the</del><lb/> the ground pepper, + grated nutmeg to be rubbed<lb/> ont he Fish. the large spice laid between<lb/> the layers of Fish. half an lb of Salt to be<lb/> stewed in. - cover them with good Vinegar. tie<lb/> them down with Paper three or four times<lb/> double bake them. + when cool cover the<lb/> Jar with a Bladder <del><gap/></del> over them. + fill the<lb/> Jar with mutton Fat. tie a bladder over the <lb/> Jar. + then a paper. - if more Vinegar is<lb/> wanted after they are baked some must<lb/> be scalded + put into the Jar. in a few<lb/> months they will be a salmon Color, +<lb/> excellent to eat. -
