56<lb/> <head>To make a <unclear>Heus</unclear> Nest. a Supper Dish</head><lb/> 99/ Fill your Shapes half full of Jelly, and let it<lb/> cool, get a few of the Smallest sized Eggshells<lb/> fill them with Blanchemange when cold brake off the<lb/> Shell lay this on the jelly with Lemon Peel cut<lb/> very small and long to resemble <unclear>strams</unclear>. then fill up<lb/> your Shape with jelly, take care it be not warm<lb/> blast it would meet the Blanchmange + + <lb/> when cold turn it out on your Dish, a few<lb/> yellow <unclear>Comfils seallard</unclear> through the Jelly would<lb/> look like wheat.-<lb/> <pb/> <head>Stuffing for a Hare.</head><lb/> 100/ An equal quantity of Beef Suet. bread grated, a little<lb/> pepper, salt, mixed parsley grated Lemon. Nutmeg<lb/> little minced thyme and onion <add>very</add> fine minced.-<lb/> wet with a little new milk- this is very light + good<lb/> have the inside of the Hare very dry. when this is<lb/> put into it.-<lb/> <pb/> To
