57<lb/> <head>To Dress Macaroni - Miss Boileau</head><lb/> <pb/> 101/ Take a quantity of a pound of Maca<hi rend="superscript">ron</hi> boil it until<lb/> tender. drain it from the water, take half a pint of<lb/> very good Gravy. the size of a small nut of butter<lb/> grate Bread. and some good Gloucester Cheese. stew<lb/> the Maca<hi rend="superscript">r</hi>. in the gravy for a little time. butter the<lb/> bottom of the Dish you intend it bake it in, lay<lb/> lay a layer of Macarony. then cover much the grated<lb/> Bread, then Cheese, then Macarony so continue<lb/> until the dish be properly filled, and bake it half<lb/> an hour, it should be brown on the top. observe<lb/> to have a layer of Cheese and Bread next the bottom<lb/> of the Dish before you put in the Macarony.<lb/> <hi rend="underline">for second course</hi> - <lb/> <pb/> <head>White Soup- very good M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Hamilton.</head><lb/> 102/ Take a Nuckle of Veal and a fowl put them<lb/> down to Boil, two or three Onions, some Mace<lb/> a little whole pepper, and about five quarts of Soft<lb/> water, boil this to one half strain it: and let it settle<lb/> Scum off all grease. then set it on the fire<lb/> to get a boil, when going to use it, and very<lb/> little before it is served up, add a pint of Rich <add>Sweet</add>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/007/001/086|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
58<lb/> Sweet Cream and the Yolks of two Eggs well beat.<lb/> and a little salt add toasted Bread cut in Sippets and<lb/> and Stuck with Almonds blanched and cut long and<lb/> thin, you may if you prefer it add Vermacelia or<lb/> Macarony this Soup should be rich jelly it must be<lb/> kept stewing one way and constantly after the egg goes<lb/> into it.-<lb/> <pb/> <head>Orange Pudding- M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Kelly</head><lb/> 103/ Beat the yolks of nine Eggs to a cream put to this<lb/> a quarter of a pound of fresh butter, the like of white<lb/> Sugar pounded, a Nutmeg, a large glass of Brandy<lb/> a little fresh grated Lemon peel, a Spoonful of Orange<lb/> rind that has been boiled up in Sugar, put all these<lb/> ingredients into a Deep Dish, and put it on Stew-<lb/> <unclear>Month</unclear>, or <unclear>Cheafing</unclear> Dish stir it one way, until it <lb/> melts thickens and becomes a clear yellow, take care<lb/> for fear it should curdle, have the Dish you intend<lb/> to bake your Pudding in ready with a rich puff paste<lb/> in it at bottom and sides. also cut candid orange in<lb/> thin long slices lay them on the paste and when just<lb/> going into the oven. pour in the pudding half an,<lb/> hour bakes it will fall. if taken out of the oven any<lb/> time before it be served up.-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

