59<lb/> <head>Force Meat Pettys</head><lb/> 104/ Mince roast or boiled fowl, two ounces of fat Bacon<lb/> the like quantity of Beef Suet minced fine, give it a little<lb/> boil mix this with your minced meat, Season this<lb/> with Lemon peel, parsley finely sliced, Suet, pepper<lb/> Nutmeg, the juice of Lemon two Spoonfuls of good <lb/> cream. make your pettys in small pans. with rich<lb/> puff paste at bottom-<lb/> <pb/> <head>Force Meat petty's. M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Field.</head><lb/> 105./ Take two ounces of veal, or white part of a fowl,<lb/> stew it in Butter, until you think it done sufficiently<lb/> boil two ounces of beef suet and the like quantity<lb/> of Bacon in water for a quarter of an hour to take<lb/> off the greasiness. steep two ounces of Bread in Milk<lb/> until quite soft. then squeeze out the milk. from the bread,<lb/> add one ounce of lean bacon. season with pepper minced<lb/> pepper, a very fine cut onion. pound all in a Marble<lb/> Mortar. until smooth and well mixed, put to this<lb/> force meat the yolks of Seven Eggs and one white<lb/> well beat. stir all together. and put into petty's which<lb/> all to have puff Paste at bottom and top. and bake them<lb/> as tarts- this is the best receipt for this Dish-<lb/> <pb/> A Green
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

