139<lb/> Pickle for two Hams. Cp: D<hi rend="superscript">o</hi>-<lb/> <pb/> Four Gallons of Water two pounds Bay salt<lb/> Four pound slock salt. Six ozs Salt Petre<lb/> Two Oz's Salt <unclear>Puenella</unclear>, two pound coarsest<lb/> Brown Sugar, Boil the whole together<lb/> for quarter of an hour skim it<lb/> <unclear>up</unclear>, pour it over the hams. at them<lb/> through for three weeks- if not<lb/> <unclear>spond</unclear> with the Pickle they must<lb/> be turned every day.<lb/> <pb/> To Cure Bacon<lb/> <pb/> To each score of pork use 4 ozs<lb/> Salt pickle. Let it be packed in<lb/> the Vessel with the skin down, +<lb/> remain three weeks <unclear>propart</unclear> with<lb/> slights - then pour pickle round<lb/> <unclear>two cages</unclear> for as <hi rend="underline">not</hi> to take the salt off<lb/> <gap/> top - let it remain a month or<lb/> two. and then hang it.-
