142<lb/> Orange Marmalade<lb/> <pb/> Weigh the Oranges + take this<lb/> weight in sugar. then cut them<lb/> into quarters + take off all the<lb/> white rind, when the peel is boiled<lb/> for tender a straw will pierce<lb/> cut it into chips- strain all<lb/> the juice, + pick the pulp<lb/> <unclear>pur</unclear> from <unclear>bon</unclear> + pippins, +<lb/> boil it with the sugar +<lb/> when it straps in Jelly from<lb/> the spoon put in the chips<lb/> + let them boil for five minutes<lb/> (Glasgow <unclear>Doccpts</unclear>,<lb/> <pb/> Lemon Pudding Bob Boyd<lb/> Pare six lemons, boil the rinds very tender<lb/> then beat them with 1/2 lb of sugar 1/4 <hi rend="underline">lb</hi> of<lb/> Butter, 14 eggs, add the juice of three Lemons<lb/> by degrees, always stirring it the same<lb/> way, Put puff paste round the edge of<lb/> The dish- Half an hour will bake it-<lb/> <pb/>
