143<lb/> To stew Pears to keep all the year<lb/> <pb/> The Pears being peeled, and split, to<lb/> 12 <hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">lbs</hi></hi> of them put one quart of strong<lb/> Cidre, one shillings worth of Cochineal<lb/> pounded very fine, some Cinnamon, <lb/> Cloves, a little Lemon peel, and 6 <hi rend="superscript">lbs</hi><lb/> of Sugar. stew them until tender,<lb/> then add as much more sugar<lb/> to the <unclear>sizup</unclear>, which, when boiled<lb/> put in your pears a several time,<lb/> 4 stew them till done <unclear>wagh</unclear><lb/> <pb/> Lemon Pudding Bob Boyd<lb/> Half a pound of sugar, one large or Two small<lb/> Lemons, grate the rinds, squeeze the juice and<lb/> mix with The sugar, eight eggs, have out <lb/> The whites of half, beat them and mix all<lb/> together, with about The size of an egg of<lb/> Butter-<lb/> <pb/>
