144<lb/> <head>Preserved Ginger</head><lb/> <pb/> Pare + cut in pieces the Nick stalks of the<lb/> Lettuce, put them in water, then give them a<lb/> boil, make a <hi rend="underline">thin</hi> syrup with white sugar + <lb/> 2 Oz of ground ginger, to 3 or 4 pound of the<lb/> Lettuce stalks, give them a boil in it + let<lb/> them stand for a day or two. boil again +<lb/> Let all stand as before. boil for the <hi rend="underline">third</hi> tin<lb/> then strain + wipe the lettuce clean, +<lb/> make a fresh syrup, scrape + add some<lb/> whole ginger to the stalks + give all a boil,<lb/> put them by for a day or two, then boil<lb/> again, again, + again, till quite clear<lb/> <add>1<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">st</hi></hi> syrup 1+1/2 lb sug<lb/>1 quart water- 2. oz<lb/>Ginger</add><lb/> <pb/> <head>Preserved, Cucumber,</head><lb/> <pb/> Pour a hot Pickle of salt + water on<lb/> the Cucumbers, when they had been 12 hours<lb/> in it, dry them very well, then boil the<lb/> Vinegar, + when it is boiling throw the <lb/> Cucumbers in + so soon as the Vinegar again<lb/> boils- let both Vinegar + Cucumbers boil for<lb/> <hi rend="underline">three</hi> minutes. then put all into a crock +<lb/> cover all close<lb/> <pb/>
