147<lb/> Orange Syrup<lb/> Select ripe + thin skinned oranges. squeeze<lb/> the juice through a sieve, to every <del>p<gap/> </del><add>pint</add><lb/> add 1 1/2 <hi rend="underline">lb</hi> of powdered sugar, boil slowly<lb/> + skin as long as any scum rises, then<lb/> take it off + when cold bottle it.<lb/> <unclear>bedwre</unclear> to <unclear>leavre</unclear> the cork well. <lb/> 2 Table spoonfuls. of this mixed in<lb/> melted butter make a nice sauce for<lb/> puddings or a small quantity improves<lb/> custards-<lb/> <head>-<unclear>Preock</unclear> Beef-</head><lb/> Make a strong pickle of 4 gals cold water<lb/> + as much salt as will make it carry an Egg<lb/> add 1 1/2 of. salt <unclear>preenel</unclear> 1/4 <hi rend="superscript">lb</hi>. salt peter<lb/> 1/2 lb. Treacle or brown Sugar, boil all together till<lb/> the pickle is quite <unclear>chan</unclear> + well leassend, let it<lb/> remain 24 hours to be quite cold the <unclear>foll</unclear> it is<lb/> put on the Beef- this quantity will <unclear>prove</unclear><lb/> 8 or 9 Pieces of. Beef
