<head>Mrs Donaldsons Receipt for a Complaint in the Bowels</head> <lb/> Take a Nutmeg roast it or toast it before the fire very slowly when<lb/> done pound it fine with as much sugar, take one half of this at <lb/> first- wash it down with a glass of <unclear>mald</unclear> Claret some time<lb/> after take the remainder in like manner.-<lb/> <pb/> <head>A Cure for Worms</head><lb/> Take <unclear>Soeominc Aloes</unclear> two Drachms, wormseed in powder one<lb/> sample. Treacle four ounces, make it into an Eldany with one<lb/> Tablspoonful of flour - If one Teaspoonful every morning gives more<lb/> than two motions the quantity must be decreased- milk must<lb/> not be used when this medicine is taking.<lb/> <pb/> <head>The Vinegar of the Four <unclear>Flueies</unclear> of Marseilles</head><lb/> Take Rue. Lavender. Wormwood. mint. sage and Rosemary of<lb/> each one handful, put them into a Gallon of Vinegar in a<lb/> Stone jar, stop it close up, let it stand by the fire six nights<lb/> then strain it off and to every Quart add three Quarts of one <lb/> ounce of Camphire. keep it corked close.- Rub your <unclear>Temples</unclear><lb/> and wash your mouth and stuff some up your Nose when<lb/> you go into a sick Room-<lb/> <pb/> A syrup
