43<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Ginger Wine</hi> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Baker<lb/> Take 2 oz of bruised Ginger to 7 Gallons<lb/> of water + 7 p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of sugar. boil them one<lb/> hour add the whites of 7 Eggs to clarify it<lb/> skim it when boil'd strain it into a<lb/> Tub and let it stand till cold, put it<lb/> into a vessel with the juice of 8 Lemon, <lb/> and the peels pounded. a spoonful of<lb/> yeast on the Top stop The Cask close<lb/> Bottle it in a fortnight<lb/> <pb/> Currant Wine - M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> C Bond<lb/> <pb/> To 3 quarts of Water one quart of Juice<lb/> to every Gallon 3 lt of sugar stir it<lb/> well together and let it stand till next<lb/> day then stir it again and the third<lb/> day skim it well in the Wine. you<lb/> must not stop it till it has done working<lb/> <pb/>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/008/001/058|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
44<lb/> To make Raisin Wine The same<lb/> Take of the best Malaga Raisins<lb/> 5 lb to a Gall<hi rend="superscript">n</hi> of Water Wine Measure<lb/> chop them small + put them into <lb/> an Open vessel boil the Water pour<lb/> <del>+</del> it on the Raisins boiling Hot<lb/> stir it well together + cover it up<lb/> very close let all stand 10 or 12 days<lb/> stirring it well every day then press<lb/> it from the Raisins + put it into<lb/> your vessel adding a 1/4 of a p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of<lb/> Clary Seed to 15 Gallons of wine.<lb/> let the vessel have some vent till<lb/> you find by the noise ceasing that<lb/> it has done fermenting then stop the<lb/> vessel very close - The Clary seed<lb/> must be <del>hung</del> put in a bag, and hung<lb/> in the wine
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/008/001/059|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
45<lb/> Grape Wine The same<lb/> <pb/> Put a quart of Water to 5 p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of Grapes<lb/> Squeeze The Grapes, boil the water +<lb/> let it stand a quarter of an hour, then<lb/> pour it on the Grapes + let it stand<lb/> 24 hours strain it off + put 4 <add>lt</add> of sugar<lb/> to every gallon of Liquor, let it stand<lb/> all night put it in your vessel + let<lb/> stand till Christmas then drain it off<lb/> and rince the Vessel with a quart of<lb/> strong Beer and put it into the Vessel<lb/> again + let it stand till Grape time<lb/> and then Bottle it<lb/> <pb/>
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/008/001/060|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
46<lb/> Orange Wine M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <unclear>Onston</unclear><lb/> boil 20 Gallons of Water + let it cool<lb/> a little have ready 112 lt of Malay<lb/> Raisins coarsely choppd then pour<lb/> on the water let it stand coverd <unclear>don</unclear><lb/> 14 Days stirring it twice a day then<lb/> strain The Liquor from The Raisins<lb/> + squeeze them very hard. let it run<lb/> through a hair sieve then <add>pare</add> <del>put</del> 100<lb/> Seville Oranges very thin squeeze<lb/> them on the Peels + put it + the<lb/> Liquor into the Vessel + when it has<lb/> done working stop it up, you may<lb/> bottle it when time. if the wine does<lb/> not fine in half a year you may<lb/> bottle it when fine. if the wine does<lb/> not fine in half a year you may<lb/> drain it off The Grounds clean, but<lb/> not wash The vessel then put in the <lb/> wine again + stop it up a month or two
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/008/001/061|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
47<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Currant Wine</hi> - The same<lb/> Strip the Currants from the Stalks and break<lb/> Them with your hands and then press<lb/> them in a hair bag + to every Gall<hi rend="superscript">n</hi><lb/> of Liquor put a p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of <unclear>Double</unclear> refind<lb/> sugar, put it into a clean cask of an<lb/> anker or 1/2 anker let it work 2 or 3<lb/> days then stop it up + set it in a <lb/> cool <sic>celar</sic> and when it is fine bottle it<lb/> <pb/> Grape Wine The same<lb/> <pb/> Put a quart of Water to 5 lt of Grapes<lb/> boil the water and let it stand a quarter <lb/> of an hour Then pour it on the Grapes<lb/> and let it stand 24 hours strain it off<lb/> + put 4 <hi rend="superscript">lt </hi> of Sugar to every Gall<hi rend="superscript">n</hi> of Liquor<lb/> let it stand all night, put it into your<lb/> vessel + let it stand till Christmas, then<lb/> drain it off + rince The vessel with a quart <lb/> of strong Beer put it into the Vessel again + let<lb/> it stand till Grape time + then bottle it -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

