49<lb/> Raisin Wine - M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Rider<lb/> <pb/> half a hundred of Smyrna Raisins<lb/> D<hi rend="superscript">o</hi> of Malaga - new - put to them when<lb/> pick'd from the large stalks, 17 Gall' of<lb/> Water, put 1 Gall of Water to the stalks<lb/> let them stand 24 hours beat them well<lb/> then strain off the Water and put it to<lb/> the Raisins let them stand 3 weeks<lb/> stir them well twice a day. press the<lb/> Fruit + put The Liquor into a Cask.<lb/> when done working keg it close +<lb/> in 6 weeks add one quart of Brandy<lb/> <pb/>
