51<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Shrewsbury Cakes</hi><lb/> Beat 1/2 a p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of Butter to a Ceram. add<lb/> half a p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of dried Flour, 1 Egg six oz of<lb/> sifted Sugar a few Caraway seeds.<lb/> mix them well roll it out thin, cut<lb/> it out with a Glass or Tin. prick them<lb/> bake them on Tins in a slack oven<lb/> <pb/> Gooseberry Cheese<lb/> <pb/> Take the rough <unclear>nd</unclear> Gooseberry when<lb/> ripe pulp them and <unclear>neak</unclear> the skins<lb/> amongst them to a p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of Fruist 1 p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of<lb/> sugar - boil it 1 hour<lb/> <pb/> <hi rend="underline">Pickle Walnut</hi><lb/> put them in Salt + Water strong enough to<lb/> <unclear>wear</unclear> an Egg for nine days. Changing the Water<lb/> every Third day cover them with white wine vinegar<lb/> put to them all kind of splices + some mustard seed<lb/> in a muslin Bag. keep them for some time upon<lb/> you use them + let them be close stoppd. the<lb/> Vinegar and spice to be boild 3 times<lb/> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <unclear>Jacomb</unclear><lb/> <pb/>
