52<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Pickled Lemon</hi> - M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Baker<lb/> 12 Lemons pared so Thin that not a<lb/> bit of the White is to be seen. slit them<lb/> across at each end work in as much salt<lb/> as you can rubbing them very well both<lb/> within and without lay them in an earthen<lb/> pot for 3 or 4 Days and strew a good deal<lb/> of salt over them. Then put in 12 Cloves<lb/> of Garlick + a large handful of Horseradish<lb/> dry the Lemons with the salt over them<lb/> in a very slow oven till the Lemons<lb/> have no moisture in them but the Garlick<lb/> and Horse radish must not be dried so<lb/> much, then take a Gall<hi rend="superscript">n</hi> of Vinegar<lb/> half an ounce of Cloves D<hi rend="superscript">o</hi> Mace D<hi rend="superscript">o</hi><lb/> Nutmegs broken roughly + 1/2 an Oz<lb/> of Kyan Pepper give them a boil up<lb/> in a Gall<hi rend="superscript">n</hi> of Vinegar and when cold<lb/> stir in a quarter of a p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of Flour of <unclear>Mustard</unclear>
