7<lb/> <hi rend="underline">Salmon Dye</hi><lb/> Spanish <unclear>Arnotto</unclear>/ abt a Shillings<lb/> worth is sufficient for small Tent<lb/> Bed/ tye it in a small Flannel Bag<lb/> and it into Copper of boiling Water<lb/> let it boil half an hour, or till you<lb/> find the water sufficiently tinged<lb/> which may be known by dipping <del>it</del><lb/> in a small PIece of Callieo. Then warm<lb/> the Callieo/ even if new/ in a strong<lb/> soap Lather and after you have taken<lb/> out the Arnetta throw it quite hot<lb/> into the the Copper moving it about the<lb/> whole time. It will appear a dirty<lb/> Orange Colour take <unclear>dot</unclear> the Callico wash<lb/> it gently in two or three waters to<lb/> wash the Soap clean out, to the last<lb/> water
