4<lb/> A pale green Wash for a Room<lb/> <pb/> 4 p<hi rend="superscript">ds</hi> of blue Vitriol of 1 p<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> of spanish<lb/> Whiting. boil these together in a Gall<hi rend="superscript">n</hi><lb/> or two of water the quantity is not<lb/> material. keep it constantly stirring<lb/> for an hour or more. let it cool, when<lb/> the whole mixture will fall to the<lb/> bottom. decant the clear water of +<lb/> then mix the rest with size made<lb/> according to the proper method. let<lb/> the Wash be laid on the Wall or Paper<lb/> in 3 or 4 Coats suffering each Coat to <lb/> dry perfectly before the next is laid on<lb/> it must be done in an earthen Pipkin<lb/> and not in any kind of metal, and<lb/> the Vitriol should be put into the<lb/> Quantity
