<head>Baking Powder</head><lb/> Flour 123<lb/> carbonate of soda 143<lb/> Tartaric acid 83<lb/> Cream of Tartar 43<lb/> all to be put in the oven and<lb/> dried except the flour when dry<lb/> put in a mortar and mix well<lb/> afterwards put it through a <lb/> wire of hair sieve- and Bottle<lb/> <hi rend="underline">it</hi> keeping it from the air.<lb/> <lb/> use a small teaspoonful to one<lb/> pound of flour for cakes<lb/> <lb/> Pastry, only half a tea-<lb/> spoonful of the powder worked<lb/> with a little batter, with cold<lb/> milk or water.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

