<head>Ginger Wine-</head> <lb/> To every Gallon of Water add two<lb/> pounds of sugar, 1 1/2 oz of Ginger, <lb/> well bruised- boil these together<lb/> for half an hour, + skim it well<lb/> (put the ginger into a linen<lb/> bag to prevent it being skimm'd<lb/> off) When nearly cold add the <lb/> juice of two Lemons, also the<lb/> rind cut very thin, to <hi rend="underline">each</hi> <lb/> <hi rend="underline">Gallon</hi>; when quite cold, put<lb/> a little yeast spread on a piece<lb/> of Toasted bread- turn it up Ginger<lb/> and al together + in about ten<lb/> days if the working has ceased<lb/> rack it off- after having rinsed<lb/> the barrel clean with a little<lb/> Brandy, return it into the barrel
