<head>Cream Cheese-</head><lb/> Take a Quart of the very best Cream<lb/> in a Bason let it stand two<lb/> nights + one day, take care to stir<lb/> it often. then take a large spooon<lb/> + lay it into a soup plate at<lb/> the top of it + le it be changed every<lb/> day-<lb/> When it is dry lay Vine or<lb/> strawberry leaves over + covered with<lb/> a <unclear>fun</unclear>- then it will be fit for <lb/> use- T Johnson-<lb/> To preserve Green Goosberries in imitation of <unclear>Raps</unclear>-<lb/> Take the largest Green Goosberries when<lb/> nearly ripe, cut them at the stalk end<lb/> in four quarters, leaving them whole<lb/> at the Blosom end, then take out<lb/> all the seeds, put five or six one<lb/> with the other, take a Needleful of
