The darker dye should not be <lb/> mixed with the Tumerick, till it<lb/> is used + if it is found of too dark<lb/> a colour, a little more spirits of wine<lb/> may be used. - - - <lb/> <hi rend="underline">Logwood stain. Brown</hi><lb/> The following is given as an<lb/> infallible cure for the bite of a<lb/> mad dog -<lb/> Take the leaves of <unclear>one</unclear>, picked<lb/> from the stalks and bruised, <lb/> six ounces garlick picked from<lb/> the stalks and bruised, Venice<lb/> treacle and <unclear>mithidate</unclear>, an a<lb/> the scraping of pewter, of each<lb/> four ounces, boil all these over<lb/> a slow fire, in two quarts of<lb/> strong all, till one be consumed
