<head>Brown Bread Pudding</head><lb/><pb/> Half a p<hi rend="underline">d</hi> of Brown Bread grated 1/2 a pound<lb/> of Currants, D<hi rend="superscript">o</hi> Beef Suet, chopp'd <hi rend="underline">very small</hi><lb/> 1/4 of a lb of powdered Sugar, the yolks of four<lb/> Eggs, a little grated nutmeg, boil it two hours<lb/> if you pout it in three small Basons should<lb/> well boil them.<lb/> <pb/> Baked Apple Dumplings-<lb/><pb/> Scoop out the Cores + pare the apples, + fill<lb/> them with orange Marmalade or what sweet<lb/> meat you please roll them up in <unclear>hot</unclear> Crust<lb/> + put them into a Dish + bake them - have<lb/> a with sauce of butter Sugar + a little beat <lb/> Cinamon- <lb/> <pb/> Lady C: B
