<head>To Fry Fish -</head> <lb/> After the fish is washed. let it be well drained<lb/> with a clean cloth, so as to drain the water well<lb/> out, then take yolks of Eggs clean from the Whites<lb/> laid pretty thick on the top, shew white bread<lb/> finely grated over the Eggs- let the fish lay<lb/> an <hi rend="underline">hour</hi> at <hi rend="underline">least</hi> before it is fried to <unclear>perm</unclear> the<lb/> Egg + <unclear>crum B</unclear> upon it, put lard to your <unclear>droping</unclear><lb/> frying pan - when boiling hot put your<lb/> fish in - when sufficiently done take it out<lb/> + lay it upon a dish before the fire a little<lb/> time to crisp + clear it from the grease, before<lb/> you send to Table - <lb/> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <unclear>Thuster</unclear>
