a stone Bottle- Before you use the yeast<lb/> boil Potatoes + bruise them thr<hi rend="superscript">o</hi> a sieve, + add to it<lb/> the Potatoes. should be mixed in the <unclear>yeast</unclear><lb/> 4 hours before it is used.<lb/> <pb/> <head>To make Currant Wine</head><lb/> 1 Stone ripe currants 3 quarts of Raspberries<lb/> 12 quarts of water. It should stand<lb/> 24 hours, and then be thrown into a <lb/> sieve to strain; afterwards run through<lb/> a bag upon a stone of sugar then barrel<lb/> it up + add bottle of Brandy, It must<lb/> not be bunged up till it has done<lb/> fermenting, add 1/2 oz of Isinglass,<lb/> if at <add>the end of</add> that time it be too sweet it<lb/> should not be bottled off- if not<lb/> it must, and also be well corked - <lb/> <pb/>
