<head>Convulsion Cakes</head> <lb/> Take half an ounce of oil of amber, <lb/> two ounces of gum oragon, soak the<lb/> gum all night in spring water, <lb/> and then prick it very clean, bruise<lb/> it well with a spoon, and add to it <lb/> a pound and a half of pineloaf sugar<lb/> work all into a paste, make it into<lb/> cakes, and dry it in the sun-<lb/> <pb/> A new born child may take seven<lb/> or eight grains increasing to fifteen<lb/> for one of three months old to twentyone,<lb/> to nine months old- thirty grains:<lb/> for a year old increasing in proportion<lb/> afterwards to 60 grains for a grown<lb/> <unclear>wh husen -</unclear>
