<head>Ginger Cakes</head> <lb/> Beat 5 Eggs with 3/4 lb of loaf sugar half an<lb/> hour <add>then add</add> 2 oz of finely powdered Ginger then<lb/> 1 <del>lb</del> of fine flour. mix but do not beat the<lb/> map after the flour is added- lay the Cakes<lb/> roughly on the tins before <del>therefore</del> baking<lb/> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Bedford approved<lb/> <head>Lemon Pudding</head><lb/> Melt 5 oz of butter in three table spoonfuls<lb/> of Cream 6 oz of loaf Sugar. Beat 8 Eggs<lb/> and 4 whites, grate the rind + squeeze the<lb/> juice of two Lemons. When the Butter is<lb/> melted stir it in the Eggs and Lemon. then<lb/> put it in a saucepan + set it on the fine<lb/> stirring it until it thickens. Put in the <lb/> Crust at the bottom of the dish + bake it. <lb/> <pb/> <head>Fish Sauce</head><lb/> A Table spoonful of an strong sauce, A table spoonful of<lb/> Lemon Pickle, half a teacup full of Beef Gravy - a<lb/> Wine Glass of Pot wine - half a teaspoonful of mace<lb/> half a teaspoonful of nutmegs, a quarter of a pound<lb/> of Butter - M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> <unclear>Cletherow</unclear> - good -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/010/001/070|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
<head>A skim milk Pudding for a rich</head> <lb/> <head>Person</head>. - <lb/> In a pint of skim milk boil a little mace<lb/> a little Lemon peel two bitter almonds<lb/> let it stand till cold then strain it + add<lb/> four large Eggs, let them be well beaten, a<lb/> little salt + sugar to your taste. twenty minutes<lb/> will boil it. let it stand a few minutes before<lb/> you thin it out of the Cup.-<lb/> The pudding Cup should be put into the<lb/> Kettle with a peak upon the cloth + a weight<lb/> upon that + boiling water <hi rend="underline">poured</hi> upon it<lb/> but not quite over the top of the pulp<lb/> Miss Derroch -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

