D<hi rend="superscript">r</hi> Scotts directions for the use of the acid Bath<lb/> set the Fluid dreg on the Skin, at the experia<lb/> tion of the 5 minutes, let the Feet be dried<lb/> + gently melted with a warm Towel.<lb/> In a few nights the skin will probably<lb/> be slightly reddened, which generally<lb/> indicates that the acids are favorally<lb/> affecting the System, let the end of <hi rend="underline">the week</hi> <lb/> the bathing should be used once every other<lb/> night + only for another fortnight; at the<lb/> expiration of that <unclear>pound</unclear> it is to be suspended<lb/> entirely for one month after which the same<lb/> course exactly is to be updated.<lb/> during the use of the acids <hi rend="underline">no</hi> preparation<lb/> <hi rend="underline">of mercury</hi> is to be taken but if the Bowels<lb/> are confined and the Acids do not act in <lb/> remaining the Bill a gentle purgative<lb/> must be taken.
