Cheap Plum Pudding. M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Clarke Sen<lb/> Quarter of a pound of Suet. quarter of a pound<lb/> of Treacle a pint of milk, as much Flour<lb/> as will make it up into a paste as thick as plum<lb/> Cake, half a pound of Currants or Raisins, <lb/> tie it tight in a Cloth + boil it four hours. <lb/> half the quantity of the ingredients will be<lb/> sufficient for a small <unclear>pudding</unclear>. a little sugar<lb/> is an infringement.
