<head>To make Raisin Wine.</head> <lb/> Eight pounds of Malaga Raisins to a Gallon of Water<lb/> Ale measure, a quarter of a pound of Hops to thirty<lb/> Gallons of Water to be boiled in it half an hour<lb/> strain the Hops out, measure the Water upon<lb/> the Raisins as hot as possible stir it well every<lb/> day till it smells strong like Wine then strain <lb/> it through a hair Bag put it into the Barrel<lb/> with the Bung on but leave the Vent Hole<lb/> open for a mouth. Plug the Barrel in half a<lb/> year and taste if it is fit for Boiling - <lb/> A Bottle of Brandy to every Ten Gallons. -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

