<head>To make Curd Cheesecake</head> <lb/> Take a Pint of Curd, six Eggs beat them<lb/> well together- a Quarter of a Pound of Currants<lb/> sweeten it to your taste - add a little Nutmeg<lb/> and Rose Water - Make a good Paste to put it <add>in</add> <lb/> <head>To make an Apple Pudding to boil</head><lb/> Take four ounces of grated Bread. four ounces<lb/> of Apples four D<hi rend="superscript">o</hi> of Currants - four Eggs - sugar<lb/> to your taste add a little Brandy- boil it an hour<lb/> <head>- To cure a Ham -</head><lb/> Take 2 ounces of Saltpetre- one ounce of <lb/> Black Pepper 1/2 a pound of white Salt-<lb/> a Pound of Bay Salt- pound all well together<lb/> Rub your Ham well with it for four Days
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/010/001/097|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
<gap/> to it <del>four</del> a pound + half of Treacle<lb/> <gap/>n it every day for a month - then put<lb/> it in water for 24 hours - then hang it to dry<lb/> Before you boil it put it in water for 24 hours<lb/> <head>To make Green Peas Soup.-</head><lb/> Take 2 quarts of strong mutton Broth- one<lb/> quart of Peas + boil in it a few whole Peppercorns<lb/> when they are boiled enough to bruise thro a Sieve<lb/> make it about the thickness of Cream- <lb/> Then take a pint of Peas six Lettuces 4 or 6<lb/> Cucumbers - 3 or 4 large Onions - a little green<lb/> fruit - Chop the herbs small - put them to<lb/> stew with a piece of Butter - a slice of Ham- <lb/> and serve it to your Taste with Pepper + Salt<lb/> when stewed enough put them to your<lb/> Soup, let it boil a quarter of an Hour -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/010/001/098|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
<head>To make a Rhubarb Cordial</head><lb/> A quart of the best old brandy.<lb/> Two tablespoonfulls of powdered Rhubarb<lb/> A small Nutmeg grated<lb/> A Teaspoonful of grated Ginger.<lb/> Two Ounces of double refined Sugar.<lb/> Mix all together in a <unclear>selw</unclear> Bowl or Cup and set it on<lb/> fire, let it brown for neer half an hour, stew it now and<lb/> then while doing - when done sufficient blow it out + when<lb/> cool bottle it - cask it lose and keep it for use.-<lb/> It is an excellent medicine for any <unclear>Suhnet</unclear> in the <unclear>Otomar</unclear><lb/> or any complaint in the bowels, or <unclear>scosful</unclear> -<lb/> A tablespoonful may be taken at any time when necessary<lb/> and <unclear>upeated</unclear> every two or three hours.-<lb/> <head>Raisin Wine -</head><lb/> Seven pounds of Raisins to an ale <del>quart</del> <add>Gally</add> of water.<lb/> The raisins picked clean from the stalks and put into the<lb/> Barrel- The water poured cold when them - stir'd thrice a<lb/> day with a stick that will reach the bottom- after it<lb/> has worked three weeks or a month put into a bottle of<lb/> Brandy- When it has done working stop it up and let<lb/> it stand three or four months, When it may be drawn off<lb/> the Cask must be formed with brimstone first). -
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

