<head>For the cure of a Green Wound +c +c +c +c +c +c</head><lb/> Dip the part with a little blue milk then put on a<lb/> little of the underneath ointment-<lb/> 1/2 a pint of sweet oil or civil oil, 4 oz of Bees Wax<lb/> 6 oz of <unclear>drachum</unclear>, and let it simmer in the oil till<lb/> dissolved. then have ready ten or eleven ounces of the best<lb/> strong in the Pot you intend to keep it in stirring it<lb/> all the while you mix it with the Honey which must<lb/> be done till it is cold or nearly so-<lb/> <head>Bread and Butter Pudding -</head> <lb/> Take a penny loaf cut it in thin slices of bread + butter<lb/> lay row in the dish- stew a few currants then a row<lb/> of bread + butter and so on till all the bread + butter is in <lb/> Take a pint of Milk, four eggs, a spoonful of brandy<lb/> a little lemon peel, and Nutmeg sweeten it to your<lb/> taste with loaf sugar- an hour will bake it-<lb/> <head>Baked Apple Pudding -</head> <lb/> Grate eight large apples put to them half a pound<lb/> of clarified butter. 3/4 of pound of sugar 6 eggs half a tea<lb/> cup full of brandy a little lemon juice lemon peel<lb/> and Nutmeg. blend them well together. Bake it with a<lb/> paste round the dish. before it goes into the oven. add<lb/> half a teacup full of cream a large one will take
