<hi rend="underline">For the Hooping Cough</hi><lb/> One ounce of Jenna, two Drachms<lb/> Rhubarb, Tartar of Vitriol Corrand<lb/> Seeds, and anise seeds of each one<lb/> Drachm, half an ounce of Liquorice<lb/> Root, and one ounce of <unclear>Lignum</unclear><lb/> <unclear>Guacacum</unclear>, Boil the ingredients<lb/> in a Pint of Water till reduced to <lb/> half the quantity strain it clear,<lb/> and add six ounces of loaf<lb/> sugar, simmer it up, + put it<lb/> in a dry Bottle - Give the Child<lb/> one spoonful Morning + night<lb/> bottling the Back with warm <lb/> Rum be full the Rive - if it should<lb/> work two in well, give a small<lb/> quantity, or miss a dose, <gap/> age<lb/> of the Child must be <unclear>candridened</unclear>, a <lb/> Table spoonful for a Child of <hi rend="underline">five</hi><lb/> years old - for a <hi rend="underline">young</hi> child a <hi rend="underline">Tea</hi><lb/> spoonful will be sufficient-<lb/> NB - The <hi rend="underline">same</hi> ingredients will<lb/> make half the quantity by adding<lb/> half a pint of water, + boiling again<lb/> + proceed as above -
