<head>To make an Omlet -</head> <lb/> Beat six Eggs (whites and yolks) very well. mix<lb/> with them a little scraped Ham, chopped Parsley,<lb/> a slave of shallot or a few Chives fine <add>chopped</add>, Pepper, Salt<lb/> <add>and</add> a <unclear>chesut</unclear> spoonful of mushroom Catchup - melt<lb/> a quarter of a pound of <unclear>Buths</unclear> in a small frying<lb/> pan, and put in the whole mixture, fry it<lb/> about four minutes, hold a hot salamander<lb/> over it for a minute to take off the raw ap-<lb/> <unclear>sprarance</unclear>, put it on your dish, folded over.<lb/> and pour over it, the butter it has been<lb/> fried in, and a little savoury gravy in the dish.<lb/>
