'[{{fullurl:TD/011/001/003|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
1.<lb/> Rich Bread Pudding<lb/> On half a pint of bread <sic>crums</sic> pour half a pint<lb/> of Scalding Milk, cover for an hour, Leak 4 Eggs +<lb/> when strained add to the bread a teaspoonful of<lb/> flour, an oz of Butter, 2 oz of sugar, <add>a few</add> half a pound of<lb/> Currants, an oz of Almonds beaten, half an oz. of <lb/> Orange, Lemon and Citron, butter a <unclear>bason</unclear> or small<lb/> cups that will exactly hold it, flour the cloth + tie<lb/> tight over it, boil one hour. Nb. it is better not<lb/> to mix the ingredients together till just before the<lb/> pudding is put in to boil - M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Rhodes<lb/> Custard Pudding<lb/> Take rather more than a pint of good milk or<lb/> Cream, let it boil 10 minutes with a with a stick<lb/> of Cinnamon, then stand till cold and add 3 Eggs<lb/> well beaten an sugar to your taste; put it through<lb/> a hair sieve, butter your dish and let bake a quarter<lb/> of an hour- M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Bennet- very good
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/011/001/004|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
2.<lb/> Lemon Pudding<lb/> Grate the rinds of three large Lemons, shred<lb/> a quarter of a pound of Almonds very fine.<lb/> pour handsful of grated Bread, about a <lb/> sauceful of shifted loaf sugar, and a 1/4 of<lb/> pound of melted Butter, + 7 or 9 Eggs, mix all<lb/> well together and add the juice of a lemon<lb/> just before putting it into the oven-<lb/> M<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Howard Standford <unclear>Shie</unclear><lb/> Boiled Egg Pudding.<lb/> One Egg, one teaspoonful of Flour, well beaten<lb/> together, half a pint of milk and a little salt.<lb/> put it into a bason and boil twenty minutes<lb/> M<hi rend="superscript">r</hi>. Key - excellent-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/011/001/005|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
3<lb/> Apple Pudding + <unclear>Chubcuks</unclear><lb/> To three ounces of Apple pared, grated or coddled and<lb/> puffed through a sieve add 3 ounces of loaf sugar<lb/> 3 Eggs well beaten, leaving out one of the whites 3 oz<lb/> of clarified <del>sugar</del> Butter, the rind of one Lemon<lb/> grated on Sugar + the juice, mix all well together<lb/> + when the Butter is cold, put it into patty tins<lb/> with a puff <unclear>yash</unclear> - Apple Pudding is made<lb/> same way <unclear>aupp</unclear> with the addition of another Egg<lb/> + 2 Ounces of Bread <sic>crums</sic>.<lb/> Almond <unclear>Whule</unclear> cakes<lb/> Two ounces of sweet Almonds, half an ounce of<lb/> Butter, one ounce of clarified Butter. half a<lb/> pound of loaf sugar, two Eggs well beaten a large<lb/> quantity of lemon peel and one teaspoonful of juice<lb/> NB half the quantity is sufficient to make at one time<lb/> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Smith Branchape
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

