4<lb/> Calf's foot jelly<lb/> Boil the rinds of four Lemons in the stock of one<lb/> set of calves feet. then add the juice of six lemons<lb/> the whites of six Eggs, one quart of pale wine 1 lt <add>of lump sugar</add><lb/> <add>or</add> sweeten to your taste and boil altogether for two or<lb/> three minutes then put into a jelly bag to clear NB<lb/> you may add a wine glass of Brandy- M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Armitage<lb/> Orange Jelly<lb/> Take three Seville Oranges and five <unclear>China</unclear>, grate<lb/> the rinds of the Seville + squeeze the juice on the<lb/> rinds, let it stand till the rest are ready; put<lb/> one pint of water to 3/4 of a pound of sugar<lb/> boil it half an hour; also boil an ounce and<lb/> half of Isinglass in a pint of water, strain them<lb/> into different basons, and when cool mix them<lb/> altogether and let it stand to stiffen.<lb/> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> M. Rhodes- very good
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/011/001/007|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
5<lb/> Restorative Jelly<lb/> Take Hartshome shavings, three quarters of a pound<lb/> Isinglass and candid Eringa root of each one ounce<lb/> + half, boil in five quarts of water to a strong jelly,<lb/> then add the juice of one Seville Orange and 1/4 of<lb/> a pound of brown sugar-candy, with half a pint of<lb/> Liston<add>re</add> Sherry wine- take half a <unclear>gie</unclear> warm, three<lb/> times a day + continue it for a long time -<lb/> Nb. a Lemon <del>will answer</del> will answer as<lb/> well as an Orange if preferred. M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Reade<lb/> Nourishing Jelly<lb/> Take one Calves foot, one quart of new milk, one<lb/> ounce of Hartshome shavings, one ounce of Isinglass,<lb/> one quart of spring water and two ounces of Sugar,<lb/> put all into a Jar, set it in the oven all night,<lb/> strain off in the morning and let a Cupful be taken<lb/> occasionally-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

