9<lb/> Primrose Vinegar<lb/> To 18 quarts of water 6 pounds of common raw sugar<lb/> half a pick of Primroses, stalks + all together, first<lb/> boil your sugar + water a quarter of an hour let it<lb/> stand till cold then put in your Primroses + 3 large<lb/> spoonfuls of yeast, let it stand in a tub 3 days, then<lb/> put it into a barrel, it must stand 6 months in a <lb/> warm place, when it has stood 2 months drain a<lb/> little out- it will make it sour later - you must<lb/> put the Primroses into a Barrel along with the Vinegar<lb/> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Rhodes receipt-<lb/> M<hi rend="underline">r</hi> Wrights receipt for washing silk stockings -<lb/> Make a good lather of boiled soap, wash the stockings<lb/> in it when ready cold changing the lather once or <lb/> twice, and fold them up very tight to squeeze out<lb/> the wet- dry. them in the air, mangle them or <unclear>shitch</unclear><lb/> them with the hand but do not- allow an Inn to touch<lb/> them- and- Never put in in <unclear>Hannd</unclear> in the manner Spoke<lb/> is <unclear>uled</unclear> will give an excellent colour to the stockings<lb/> <unclear>mote</unclear> shawls are washed in the same way
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

