To preserve ripe Melon.<lb/> <hi rend="underline">to imitate Ginger-</hi><lb/> Pare of the rind- take out the seeds + cut<lb/> the Melon into small pieces- let it lie in<lb/> salt + water two days - then put it into<lb/> fresh water for three days changing it two<lb/> or three times a day- take some of the <lb/> best white Ginger- scrape off the outside put<lb/> it into a syrup and pour it upon the melon<lb/> boiling hot - do this for two or three days<lb/> together then add more sugar till the syrup<lb/> is of a proper thickness for keeping - Cut<lb/> the fruit boil in the syrup ten minutes<lb/> and when cold put it into pots (or glass<lb/> jars for use - to every pint of syrup put<lb/> the rind of a Lemon pared thin + cut <lb/> into lengths the breadth of a straw- it should<lb/> be kept a year before it is used-<lb/> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Walker - Ferham - <lb/> 1816-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

