To preserve Wine Sauces.<lb/> <lb/> Take the finest you can get, pick off<lb/> the stalks, run down the seam only<lb/> skin deep, then take half their weight<lb/> of loaf sugar pounded, and lay it between<lb/> your plums in layers till your jar is<lb/> full, set them in a kettle of boiling water<lb/> till they are soft, thin drain the syrup<lb/> from them, and give it a boil + pour<lb/> it on them, do so for several times,<lb/> till you see the skin look hard + the<lb/> plums dear, let them stand a week,<lb/> then take them out one by one, +<lb/> put them with glasses, jars or pots,<lb/> give your syrup a boil, if you have<lb/> not sufficient, boil a little clarified sugar<lb/> with your syrup + fill up your glases with it<lb/> put brandy paper over, + tie a bladder over<lb/> to keep out the air or they will turn purple-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

