Nitre-<lb/> Nitre may be <unclear>giam</unclear> in <unclear>greed</unclear> or Whey, when it<lb/> is describable to produce perspiration- half a<lb/> Teaspoonful is the usual quantity but a <lb/> perspiration is not entirely produced them<lb/> give a teaspoonful.- M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Hind. June 23<hi rend="superscript">d</hi>- <lb/> 1830-<lb/> <pb/> A remedy on Swallowing Pins or Fish bones<lb/> 4 grains of <unclear>Sarter Emetie</unclear> dissolved in warm<lb/> water; immediately after you have taken<lb/> it, swallow the whites of 6 Eggs w<gap/>beaten-<lb/> This has been tried with wonderful success<lb/> + the pins so - have returned with the<lb/> coagulated <unclear>snass</unclear>, + the sufferer has been<lb/> relieved. - M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Hind June 23<hi rend="superscript">d</hi>- 1830-<lb/> <pb/> For the Piles-<lb/> One oz + 1/2 of flour of Brimstone 1/2 an oz of<lb/> Cream of Tarter or purified nitre 1/2 an Oz: of<lb/> <unclear>Lenitine Electuarey</unclear>, mixed together with <unclear>sinkle</unclear><lb/> syrup, take a teaspoonful night + morning-<lb/> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Hind - June 23- 1830<lb/> <pb/> For a Sore Mouth-<lb/> Equal quantities of Boll <unclear>armormives</unclear> + Aleem<lb/> mixed with Honey, + applied with a feather<lb/> to the mouth of a Child.- M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Hind June 23<hi rend="superscript">d</hi><lb/> 1830-
