Fresh Cream-.<lb/> Boil the rind of a Lemon in a pint of Cream,<lb/> squeeze the juice, + mix with it a small table<lb/> spoonful of Flour, then pour the Cream boiling<lb/> upon the juice, sweeten, + mix them well together,<lb/> then put either Cake or preserved fruits in the<lb/> bottom of the <add>Glass</add> Dish <del>or Glasses</del> + pour the Cream,<lb/> when nearly cold, upon it you may then<lb/> either ornament it or not, <unclear>flut</unclear> macroons<lb/> may be put in the top when quite cold + stiff<lb/> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> I. M. Rhodes. June 1831.<lb/> <pb/> Treatment of Neapolitan Violets<lb/> The Roots are to be put into the open ground<lb/> a foot apart + must remain so till August<lb/> when they must be put into good mould under<lb/> a glass flame with add<hi rend="underline">n</hi> of a little <unclear>Macoore</unclear><lb/> Miss Maudslay-June 1831.<lb/> <pb/> Lemon Drops<lb/> One pound of fine lump sugar beat +<lb/> sifted, the whites of 5 new laid Eggs, the juice<lb/> of one Lemon + the rind grated, beat altogether<lb/> with a whisk <hi rend="underline">half an hour</hi>, drop them on<lb/> <unclear>widing</unclear> paper dusted with sugar. Bake them<lb/> in a slow oven. you may make them silar<lb/> by adding a little cochineal + heating them<lb/> a little more - f<hi rend="underline">or</hi> Miss Rhodes- Spring Lord
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/011/001/025|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
Goosberry Cakes-.<lb/> Gather the finest Goosberries when full grown.<lb/> but not ripe put them in a jar + as then in a <lb/> pan of water on the fire till soft, pulp them<lb/> through a sieve, to a lt of pulp put a lt of sifted<lb/> sugar + the white of an Egg, heat the whole with<lb/> a whisk two hours till of a froth; drop it on<lb/> paper + set them to dry in a warm place +<lb/> keep them dry in <unclear>lous</unclear>-. (M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> A Rhodes <lb/> Horsforth<lb/> <pb/> <unclear>Whitoocth Cakee</unclear>-<lb/> One drachm of Camphor bruised in a<lb/> Master dissolve in half a pint of Spirits of<lb/> Wine 1 oz of essential oil of origanum colour it<lb/> with Alkanct root-. For sprains, bruises, cuts<lb/> so eternally- + 12 or 15 drops on a lump of sugar<lb/> for Calir-. (M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Cl R. Horsforth<lb/> <pb/> Salves for Cuts, Bruises + Boils-.<lb/> <del>Take</del> <add>Set</add> 1/2 a pint of <unclear>Saletd</unclear> Oil on the fire, shave<lb/> into it 4 oz of Bees wax + 6 ozs of <unclear>Diachipom</unclear> of <unclear>Guinea</unclear><lb/> let them simmer till they are dissolved <add>stirring them all the time</add> put 10 ozs<lb/> of Honey into a pot + pour upon it the other<lb/> ingredients + continue to stir it till it is cold<lb/> (M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> A. R. Hosforth<lb/> <pb/> Cough Medicine-.<lb/> <unclear>Bhue</unclear>, Hyssop, Horehound, each a handful boil in a<lb/> quart of water till reduced to a pint, strain it, add a lb. of<lb/> lace sugar + boil to a thick syrup, add a little vinegar<lb/> if the constitution will bear it-. (M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> A. R. Horsforth
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

