Rice + Apple Pudding as at <unclear>Christile</unclear><lb/> Take a plain baked fine pudding + fire<lb/> a dish with alternate layers of <unclear>Eree</unclear> +<lb/> apples that have been previously<lb/> boiled, cover it with a thin layer of<lb/> the whites of Eggs that have been previously<lb/> very well beaten up with as much<lb/> fine sugar as the taste of the cook<lb/> dictates put it into the oven for a<lb/> few minutes to brown, it sh<hi rend="underline">d</hi> be quite<lb/> crisp- If you wish yr pudding rather<lb/> rather takes the yolks of the Eggs that have<lb/> been previously used for the top of the<lb/> pudding + mix them with the Eiee<lb/> 2 Eggs are sufficient for a good ligid<lb/> Pudding- Miss Rhodes<lb/> Thirskill Dut-1831<lb/> Pickled Pork as brought from Butcher or Poulterer at<lb/> Brighton his <hi rend="underline">receipt-. by M<hi rend="superscript">r</hi> Brown</hi>. 1832.<lb/> Salt with fine salt as soon as cut up. rub well in<lb/> them put into a tub + cover over entirely with strong<lb/> salt + water. then put on a layer. stone or weight<lb/> + let it remain about a week. Ns salt petre or<lb/> Bay Salt-.
