Grandmama Smiths recipt for Cowslip Wine<lb/> X Cowslip Wine-<lb/> To 5 Gallons of water take 12 <unclear>lts</unclear> 1/2 of lump<lb/> sugar when near boiling put in the whites of<lb/> 4 Eggs + the rinds of 3 lemons, let all boil together<lb/> 1/2 an hour, skim it very well. then pour it upon<lb/> 2 picks lip of peeps, let stand till cold, + then<lb/> add 3 spoonful of yeast + the juice of 5 lemons,<lb/> let it stand 5 days then squeeze 3 parts of the<lb/> peeps out + put the rest along with the lome into<lb/> a cask adding one oz of Isinglass, let stand a<lb/> month, <hi rend="underline">if fi</hi>ne, bottle it- put into each bottle<lb/> a lump of sugar + a spoonful of Brandy-<lb/> NB The Lemons, yeast be must be <hi rend="underline">fresh + g</hi>ood<lb/> + the <add>pulp of the</add> former not put into the wine, as it soon<lb/> contracts any bad tast- (excellent)<lb/> <pb/> Elderberry Wine.-<lb/> Two quarts of water to one quart Berries, this must<lb/> be well boiled for a quarter of an hour or more<lb/> then squeeze the berries + strain the liquor through<lb/> a cloth; to every gallon of it, put 4 pounds of moist<lb/> sugar then boil altogether with a quarter of a<lb/> pound of allspice, Ginger, Cloves, + a few<lb/> nutmegs.- M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> S. Niclson. Roundhay Park.-<lb/> April 19<hi rend="underline">th</hi> 1834.
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

