To make a Round of Beef Red.-<lb/> Take a round of Beef, rub it with 2 oz of salt petre, let it stand<lb/> 6 hours, then rub it with 2 oz allspice very well, the same of<lb/> Pepper 1/2 lb brown Sugar + a good deal common salt,<lb/> let it stand for a fortnight, rubbing + turning it every<lb/> day before the fire, then put it in a dish pot or some-<lb/> thing that will hold it. put 4 lb<hi rend="underline">s</hi> of cut suet under +<lb/> over it, cover it with a coarse paste, set it in an<lb/> oven, fit for baking coarse head, it will take 8 hours<lb/> baking + will keep 8 months. f<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">rm</hi> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Nickelson's book<lb/> <pb/> <unclear>Fragumke</unclear> steaks.-<lb/> Take 6 bones from the best end of a large neck of mutton<lb/> take the meat from the bones, take off the skin + some of<lb/> the fat, take a little from the <unclear>niccle</unclear> until you can stewer<lb/> then quite round, beaten them with pepper, salt,<lb/> nutmeg, + mace, broil or fry them quick, put a <unclear>pan</unclear> +<lb/> white sauce in the dish, then lay the flakes upon<lb/> the sauce; some wine French beans, or Springe<lb/> looks very pretty under the steaks. frm Mrs Nickelsen's book<lb/> <pb/> an excellent Fish Sauce.-<lb/> Take a quart of red wine. one pound of anchovies, half a <lb/> pint of Vinegar, a 1/4 of an Oz of Mace, 1/4 oz Cloves, some onion<lb/> + some lemon peel. boil all these together gently over a slow<lb/> fire till about half a pint is consumed then strain it off,<lb/> when cold, put it into a bottle for use.- to 1/2 lb Butter, beat
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

'[{{fullurl:TD/011/001/034|action=edit}} Click Here To Edit]''' <!-- ENTER TRANSCRIPTION BELOW THIS LINE -->
3 spoonfuls of Sauce, put both together <hi rend="underline">cold</hi> + keep continually<lb/> stirring it, as it boils till it is as thick as you would have <lb/> it, thick it will be without flour. - f<hi rend="superscript">rm</hi> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi> Nicholsen's book.<lb/> So every gallon of goosberries full grown clean picked<lb/> + bruised put one quart of water, let it stand 5 days<lb/> stirring it twice a day, to every gallon of juice, when<lb/> strained, put 3 lbs of loaf sugar, then to every 20 quarts <lb/> of liquor all a like Brandy + a like Isinglass, Barrel<lb/> it, in half a year bottle it - if the <unclear>sweetings</unclear> is gone off.-<lb/> f<hi rend="superscript"><hi rend="underline">rm</hi> M<hi rend="superscript">rs</hi>. Nicholsen's book.-<lb/> <pb/> Apple Jelly-<lb/> Take a good quantity of apples pare + core them,<lb/> put them intoa stew pan with water enough to <lb/> prevent them becoming, when well boiled throw<lb/> them into a Jelly bag, let the juice run through<lb/> without squeezing the bag, to every quart of juice<lb/> add a pound of <add>loaf</add> sugar + Lemon put if agreeable, boil<lb/> the whole like Currant Jelly, add the juice of one<lb/> Lemon put some of the pips to colour it in the <lb/> first boiling-. f<hi rend="underline">rm</hi> M<hi rend="underline">rs</hi> Nicholsen's book-<lb/> <pb/> Pot Salmon<lb/> Steep it an hour in vinegar, then take it out, +<lb/> season it with pepper, salt, cloves, mace + nutmeg<lb/> bake it with as much fresh water as will cover it, when<lb/> cold take it out, beat it well, put it in pots + cover<lb/> it with clarified butter.-
<!-- DO NOT EDIT BELOW THIS LINE --> {{Metadata:{{PAGENAME}}}}

